ng similar types—each batch labels more spans as its available types, inflating the false positive count and dropping precision more than recall improves, which is exactly what I'm seeing in the metrics where single-batch performance shows much lower precision than recall.\n\nWith k=8 batches of roughly 8 types each, I'd expect per-batch recall around 0.45 and unique true positives from the union maybe around 0.50, but the false positive rate depends on how much each batch over-predicts relative to the gold standard.\n\nLooking at the count curve data, if each batch has a pred/gold ratio between 1.5-2.0 (falling between count_6's 2.1 and count_12's 0.9), then merging 8 batches would accumulate a lot of false positives, bringing merged precision down to roughly 0.20-0.25. That would give an F1 around 0.315, which is about a 10 percentage point drop from the single-pass approach—worse than I'd want.\n\nLet me work through the numbers more carefully using the actual count curve values. I'm realizing my logic was flawed—each batch only extracts entities of its assigned types, so for any gold entity, only one batch can correctly identify it. The merged recall should match what we see at count_8, since each batch operates with 8 types in its prompt.\n\nFor precision, the critical issue is type-2 errors: when confusable types are split across batches, the model might mislabel an entity as a type that exists in its batch but not the correct type. These mislabelings count as false positives in the merged result, whereas in single-pass extraction both types would be available for correct labeling, making SDGD precision worse overall.\n\nNow I'm working through the math to see how much precision drops. If SDGD achieves that higher recall of 0.42 but the F1 score falls to 0.364, I can back-calculate the precision by solving the F1 formula, which gives me around 0.321. So SDGD trades precision for recall—a significant drop that explains the worse F1 performance.\n\nFor random batching with the same batch size, I'm thinking through how accidentally grouping confusable types together would help the model discriminate between them. This should give random batching a slight edge over SDGD since some batches would naturally co-locate those problematic pairs, reducing false positives from type confusion.\n\nWhen I compare SDGD and random directly, the difference is minimal—only about 0.8 percentage points, well within the noise range.\n\nNow looking at per-type batching where each batch contains just one type, the recall stays high around 0.64 since each type's entities appear in only one batch, but precision tanks to 0.216 because the model over-extracts aggressively when it only sees one type. This puts per-type batching in the worst tier alongside single-pass, both significantly underperforming random batching.\n\nThe real insight here is that decomposition by type actually hurts performance—smaller batch sizes force the model to over-extract, destroying precision without enough recall gains to compensate. Single-pass with all types together turns out to be the best approach because the model needs to see confusable types simultaneously to properly discriminate between them.\n\nNow I'm checking the MAVEN setup: with 168 types and very high homogeneity, the adaptive threshold of τ=0.85 might create too many or too few batches depending on how the embeddings distribute. I need to verify the SCS statistics from the experiment registry to make sure I'm using the right numbers for MAVEN before finalizing the YAML configuration. So with the adaptive threshold τ = mean + k×std, I get τ = 0.2161 + 0.103 = 0.319 for MAVEN with Qwen3, which would make the graph extremely dense since almost every pair exceeds it—leading to many colors, many batches, and severe fragmentation. But looking at the actual SCS statistics (mean 0.2161, std 0.103, max 0.8368), these cosine similarities are surprisingly low compared to Few-NERD's mean of 0.7837, suggesting MAVEN's event types are much more semantically distinct.\n\nWith this threshold, only about 5-10% of pairs fall above τ (between q90=0.3457 and q95=0.3892), which gives a moderately connected graph with roughly 12 batches of about 14 types each. That would yield a relaxed F1 around 0.16, but I'm noticing MAVEN's relaxed F1 performance doesn't quite match what I'd expect from this batch structure.\n\nLooking at the actual performance curve, relaxed F1 increases consistently with more types—jumping from 0.106 at count_1 up to 0.247 at count_44. This is the opposite pattern from Few-NERD, which means decomposing MAVEN into smaller batches would actually hurt performance. With 12 batches of 14 types each, the merged recall would collapse since each batch only covers about 8% of the full type space. I'm realizing the merged recall should actually reflect the combined coverage across all batches—since each batch handles different types, the overall recall depends on how well each batch performs with its subset of types in the prompt. Looking at the performance curve, with around 14 types per batch, the relaxed F1 sits around 0.16, which should be roughly comparable to the merged result since we're averaging performance across batches weighted by their gold entity distributions.\n\nNow checking the actual numbers: MAVEN with SDGD-zero shows a relaxed F1 of about 0.160 compared to single-pass at 0.245, which is a drop of roughly 8.5 percentage points—that's a significant 35% relative decline. This aligns with the expected worst-tier range where the delta should fall between -8 and -3 percentage points, and similar patterns hold across other datasets like Few-NERD where a -5pp drop from 0.414 gives 0.364.\n\nLet me compile the full results across both datasets to see the complete picture.\n\nLooking at the performance metrics, decomposition consistently hurts performance—SDGD performs no better than random baselines, and the effect is especially pronounced on MAVEN where the model needs access to many event types for context. For the full MAVEN study in exp-004, I'm tracking several analyses including count curves, within-count correlations, pairwise comparisons, and per-type breakdowns, with initial results confirming the negative findings from partial runs.\n\nThe correlation analyses paint a clear picture: BCS shows either weak or zero correlation with relaxed F1 across most conditions, with MiniLM embeddings being the only bright spot at r=0.120. Per-type analysis reveals a centrality confound, and confusion rate ratios are modest at best. For DocRED, the document-level complexity of the task appears to overwhelm any confusability signal—the count curve shows flat or weakly increasing F1 similar to MAVEN, and BCS correlations aren't significant, though this experiment may not run given the tight deadline. The 2x2 interaction experiment is still in progress.\n\nFor the error taxonomy work, I'm classifying false positives into substitution errors, boundary errors, false negatives, and hallucinations, then binning by BCS. Type substitution shows a modest elevation in high-BCS bins (3-5x for extreme cases, 1.3-1.8x for random), but boundary errors and false negatives dominate the overall error distribution, suggesting confusability is only a minor contributor to the failure modes.\n\nThis isn't strong enough to establish confusability as a dominant channel in the multi-channel model. When I look at the LLaMA-3.3-70B results on the Few-NERD protocol, the pairwise correlation is essentially zero (r=0.04, p=0.07) and per-type analysis shows no significant relationship either (ρ=-0.08, p=0.54). LLaMA might simply handle confusable types differently due to its instruction tuning and scale, or the model's overall extraction quality is so poor that confusability effects get buried in the noise. I'm wondering whether LLaMA's baseline performance is just too weak across the board for any confusability signal to emerge.\n\nLooking at LLaMA's actual performance on Few-NERD with the full 66-type schema, it achieves around F1 0.35-0.40, slightly below Qwen3's 0.414. The worst-tier results show a confusion rate ratio of only 2.5x compared to Qwen3's 10-28x range, which suggests confusability effects are highly model-dependent rather than universal phenomena.\n\nFor the SCS validation experiment, I need to check how well the embedding-based confusion proxy correlates with the actual empirical confusion matrix from the calibration run. The correlation is weak at ρ=0.12 with p=0.03, barely reaching significance—this explains why the zero-shot SDGD approach fails, since it relies on this embedding proxy that doesn't capture real model confusion patterns well.\n\nNow I'm ready to compile the comprehensive results into a structured format with the key comparison tables and statistical findings. I'm settling on the YAML structure with proper formatting—each experiment will have name, plan_id, description, expected_results, result_rationale, tables, figures_description, and analysis fields to capture how the worst-tier results support the narrative shift. Now I'm writing out all 12 experiments with specific metrics and detailed explanations for how each one demonstrates the worst-tier performance pattern. The within-count correlations on MAVEN show positive relationships between relaxed F1 and BCS across different count bins—count_6 at r=+0.18 (p=0.18), count_12 at r=+0.12 (p=0.32), and pooled partial r=+0.14 (p=0.11)—none reaching significance, but all pointing in the opposite direction from Few-NERD. The confusion rate ratios on extreme batches are notably lower here (4-7x versus Few-NERD's 10-28x), which aligns with the centrality confound: high-BCS batches on MAVEN tend to contain more central and common entity types that the model handles more reliably. Now I'm going to structure the results cleanly with abbreviated metric names for brevity.\n\nLooking at the tier definitions more carefully: the worst tier specifies confusion_rate_ratio_extreme between 3-10x, meaning Few-NERD should drop from its current 10-28x down to around 3-5x with LLaMA, MAVEN to 4-7x, and DocRED to 2-4x. For cross-task significance, only 1-2 task×embedding combinations should show significant results (currently Qwen3×FewNERD and MiniLM×MAVEN), with no new ones emerging in the worst tier. The cross_model_significant constraint limits it to just 1 model showing significant results overall.\n\nNow I'm writing out the YAML configuration and verifying all 12 planned experiments are accounted for before finalizing the output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14331,"cache_read_input_tokens":43817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6066cd7-3b7c-4597-bdab-f4c39ace5902","uuid":"07acd7cf-ea94-4a66-b810-0806b0d0f0f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LgY96UuFHxfmEcr9hsjwBg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完全放弃 SDGD 方法贡献。论文 reframe 为纯系统性实证分析：首次控制实验揭示\n  schema complexity 不是一维问题——count 和 confusability 通过正交通道降低性能，\n  但 confusability 信号高度依赖模型和 embedding 选择。pairwise confusability 是\n  比 per-type 聚合更鲁棒的度量，但仅在特定 model×embedding×schema 组合下显著。\n  centrality confound 发现本身是方法论贡献。模型特异性（Qwen3 vs LLaMA）reframe\n  为 \"confusability effects are model-dependent\"——将弱点转为解释力。论文结构改为\n  \"question→controlled experiments→findings→implications\"。EMNLP Findings 是现实\n  预期，Main 可冲但 acceptance variance 大。SDGD 降为 appendix 中的 negative result\n  case study，正文不再作为核心贡献。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-004: MAVEN 全量 confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN Event Detection（168 event types, FrameNet hierarchy）的完整 confusability\n      研究：500-sample 重跑 count curve + within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise/per-type\n      双 embedding 分析 + confusion rate 分析。核心跨任务（NER→ED）验证。\n    expected_results:\n      # Count curve (500 samples, V2 prompt, relaxed matching)\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.098\n        count_6: 0.112\n        count_12: 0.155\n        count_22: 0.192\n        count_44: 0.238\n        count_64: 0.241\n        count_100: 0.243\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.008\n        count_6: 0.005\n        count_12: 0.011\n        count_22: 0.016\n        count_44: 0.021\n        count_64: 0.018\n      count_curve_recall_trend: \"monotonically increasing 0.07→0.19 (opposite of Few-NERD)\"\n      count_curve_precision_trend: \"roughly flat 0.15-0.40, noisy\"\n      # Within-count BCS-relaxed_F1 correlation (key new analysis)\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_6:\n          r: 0.175\n          p: 0.185\n          n: 27\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n        count_12:\n          r: 0.124\n          p: 0.315\n          n: 27\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: 0.142\n          p: 0.108\n          n: 54\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n      # Pairwise SCS-confusion (reconfirmation with 500 samples)\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.009\n        pearson_p: 0.38\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.115\n        pearson_p: 2.1e-42\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        spearman_rho: 0.128\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.185\n        verdict: PASS\n      # Per-type analysis (reconfirmation)\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.195\n        p: 0.018\n        direction: positive_confounded\n      per_type_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.212\n        p: 0.009\n        direction: positive_confounded\n      # Confusion rate ratios\n      confusion_rate_extreme:\n        count_6_ratio: 5.8\n        count_12_ratio: 4.2\n      confusion_rate_random:\n        count_6_ratio: 1.4\n        count_12_ratio: 1.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 event types 全部来自 FrameNet，同一语义域，导致 type embedding\n      分布高度同质。这造成三个后果：(1) count curve 反转——更多 types 为模型提供更\n      丰富的 event ontology 上下文，帮助模型理解每个 type 在 taxonomy 中的位置，因此\n      F1 随 count 增加而上升；(2) within-count BCS 相关为正方向——高 BCS batch 包含\n      语义中心的常见 event types（如 Killing, Attack, Movement），这些 types 在\n      training data 中频次高、定义清晰，LLM 本就擅长提取，因此高 BCS → 高 F1，\n      这是 centrality confound 而非 confusability 效应；(3) confusion rate 比\n      Few-NERD 低得多（5.8x vs 27.5x），因为 event trigger 本身是 verb/nominalization\n      而非 entity mention，type confusion 的表现形式不同（trigger 共享率高但不一定是\n      confusability 导致）。pairwise MiniLM 仍显著（r=0.115, p≈0），因为 n=14028 pair\n      提供了极大统计功效，即使效应量小也能检出——但这个 r 值比 Few-NERD 的 0.156 低，\n      且 Qwen3 pairwise 完全不显著，说明 pairwise 信号在同质 schema 上高度依赖\n      embedding 选择。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Count Curve (500 samples, relaxed matching)\n        | Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision | Pred/Gold |\n        |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n        | 1     | 0.098     | 0.008    | 0.070  | 0.162     | 0.43      |\n        | 6     | 0.112     | 0.005    | 0.085  | 0.165     | 0.52      |\n        | 12    | 0.155     | 0.011    | 0.118  | 0.226     | 0.52      |\n        | 22    | 0.192     | 0.016    | 0.148  | 0.274     | 0.54      |\n        | 44    | 0.238     | 0.021    | 0.180  | 0.350     | 0.51      |\n        | 64    | 0.241     | 0.018    | 0.182  | 0.358     | 0.51      |\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Within-Count BCS-F1 Correlation\n        | Count | r     | p     | Direction | Verdict |\n        |-------|-------|-------|-----------|---------|\n        | 6     | +0.175| 0.185 | positive  | FAIL    |\n        | 12    | +0.124| 0.315 | positive  | FAIL    |\n        | Pooled| +0.142| 0.108 | positive  | FAIL    |\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-Type (2×2 embedding matrix)\n        |          | Pairwise r (p)         | Per-type ρ (p)       |\n        |----------|------------------------|----------------------|\n        | Qwen3    | -0.009 (0.38) ✗        | +0.195 (0.018) ✗     |\n        | MiniLM   | +0.115 (2.1e-42) ✓     | +0.212 (0.009) ✗     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN count curve (relaxed F1 vs type count) — 上升趋势，与 Few-NERD 相反\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN pairwise scatter (MiniLM SCS vs confusion count) — 弱正相关 r=0.115，点云密集在低相似度区域\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN per-type scatter (mean BCS vs F1) — 正方向，标注 centrality confound interpretation\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 结果确认 centrality confound 假说：在语义同质 schema 中，per-type 和\n      within-count batch-level 分析均被 confound。唯一存活的信号是 MiniLM pairwise\n      (r=0.115)，但 Qwen3 pairwise 失败，且效应量小（r²=1.3%）。MAVEN 的 count curve\n      反转是对 SDGD 方法的致命打击——如果更多 types 在 prompt 中反而帮助模型，那么\n      decomposition（减少 types）必然降低性能。worst tier 叙事中，MAVEN 作为\n      \"centrality confound case study\" 仍有方法论价值，但不支持 SDGD 的前提假设。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-005: DocRED confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED（96 relation types）上的 confusability 研究：count curve + BCS 相关分析。\n      文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_4: 0.185\n        count_8: 0.192\n        count_16: 0.198\n        count_32: 0.203\n        count_48: 0.208\n        count_96: 0.195\n      count_curve_trend: \"near-flat with slight peak at count_48, no clear monotonic pattern\"\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_8:\n          r: 0.032\n          p: 0.62\n          verdict: FAIL\n        count_16:\n          r: -0.058\n          p: 0.48\n          verdict: FAIL\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: -0.015\n          p: 0.84\n          verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: 0.023\n        pearson_p: 0.14\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.031\n        pearson_p: 0.08\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        verdict: FAIL\n      per_type_bcs_f1:\n        spearman_rho: -0.04\n        p: 0.72\n        verdict: FAIL\n      confusion_rate_extreme_ratio: 1.8\n      overall_baseline_f1: 0.195\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 是文档级 RE，每个样本包含多个句子和多个 entity pairs。性能瓶颈完全不在\n      type confusability 上，而在于：(1) 跨句推理能力——关系证据分散在多个句子中，LLM\n      需要 coreference 和 multi-hop reasoning；(2) entity pair 组合爆炸——文档中 n\n      个实体产生 O(n²) 个候选关系对，模型必须处理大量负样本；(3) 关系类型定义本身\n      依赖 entity type 约束（如 \"place_of_birth\" 要求 subject=person, object=location），\n      这种结构化约束比 embedding 相似度更能预测性能。confusability 信号被这些更强的\n      因素完全淹没。count curve 近乎平坦，因为文档级 RE 的 prompt 长度主要由文档内容\n      （而非 type 定义）决定——96 个 relation type name 只占 prompt 的很小比例。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: DocRED Count Curve (document-level RE)\n        | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision | Confusion Rate |\n        |-------|-------|--------|-----------|---------------|\n        | 4     | 0.185 | 0.145  | 0.256     | 0.008         |\n        | 8     | 0.192 | 0.152  | 0.261     | 0.012         |\n        | 16    | 0.198 | 0.158  | 0.264     | 0.015         |\n        | 32    | 0.203 | 0.165  | 0.258     | 0.018         |\n        | 48    | 0.208 | 0.170  | 0.261     | 0.019         |\n        | 96    | 0.195 | 0.160  | 0.250     | 0.022         |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocRED count curve — near-flat, 与 Few-NERD/MAVEN 的明显趋势形成对比\"\n      - \"Fig: DocRED within-count BCS scatter — 无相关，点云随机分布\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 结果是完全的 null result。confusability 假说在文档级 RE 上完全不成立。\n      worst tier 叙事中，DocRED 证明 confusability 效应受限于 sentence-level 任务——\n      文档级任务中其他复杂度维度（跨句推理、entity pair 组合）占主导。如果论文要报告\n      此结果，需要 reframe 为 \"boundary condition\"：confusability 效应在 type\n      definitions 占 prompt 显著比例的任务中才成立。但此实验为 P1，worst tier 下可能\n      不运行（10 天内优先 P0 实验），视为 supplementary material。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-006: 2×2 Interaction Effect\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2 因子设计。\n      检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应（additive vs multiplicative）。\n    expected_results:\n      cell_means_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.348\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.312\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.298\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.255\n      two_way_anova:\n        count_main_effect:\n          F: 7.82\n          p: 0.008\n          eta_sq: 0.14\n          verdict: SIGNIFICANT\n        bcs_main_effect:\n          F: 2.93\n          p: 0.094\n          eta_sq: 0.06\n          verdict: MARGINAL\n        interaction:\n          F: 0.31\n          p: 0.582\n          eta_sq: 0.006\n          verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      n_batches_per_cell: 12\n      total_n: 48\n      simple_effects:\n        bcs_at_low_count:\n          delta_f1: -0.036\n          p: 0.22\n        bcs_at_high_count:\n          delta_f1: -0.043\n          p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      2×2 设计的统计功效受限：每个 cell 约 12 个 batch，总 n=48。在这个样本量下，\n      检测交互效应需要 η²≥0.10 的大效应量。实际中，count 的主效应最强（η²=0.14），\n      因为 count 直接影响 prompt 长度和 attention 分配，信号最清晰。BCS 主效应仅为\n      marginal（p=0.094），因为 batch-level BCS 与 F1 的关系本就受到 type frequency\n      distribution 等 confound 的干扰——exp-002 已经表明 batch-level 信号远弱于\n      pairwise-level。交互效应完全不显著（p=0.582），说明 count 和 confusability 的\n      联合效应是（弱）加性的，不存在 multiplicative synergy。这在 worst tier 中意味\n      着论文只能声称 \"两个通道可能独立\" 但无法用 formal interaction test 支撑。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: 2×2 Cell Means (F1, text_match)\n        |                | Low BCS     | High BCS    | BCS Effect |\n        |----------------|-------------|-------------|------------|\n        | Low Count (6)  | 0.348       | 0.312       | Δ=-0.036   |\n        | High Count (22)| 0.298       | 0.255       | Δ=-0.043   |\n        | Count Effect   | Δ=-0.050   | Δ=-0.057   |            |\n      - |\n        Table: Two-Way ANOVA Results\n        | Source       | F     | p     | η²    | Verdict     |\n        |-------------|-------|-------|-------|-------------|\n        | Count        | 7.82  | 0.008 | 0.14  | Significant |\n        | BCS          | 2.93  | 0.094 | 0.06  | Marginal    |\n        | Count × BCS  | 0.31  | 0.582 | 0.006 | NS          |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (F1 vs count, separate lines for low/high BCS) — 近似平行线，无交互\"\n      - \"Fig: Cell means bar chart with error bars — BCS 差异在两个 count level 上方向一致但均不显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      交互效应不显著是 worst tier 对 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）的重大打击。\n      论文无法用 formal factorial design 证明两通道正交。只能退而求其次，基于 error\n      taxonomy（exp-007）做 descriptive argument：count 降低 recall（omission），\n      confusability 增加 type confusion（substitution），两类错误机制不同→暗示正交。\n      但这种 descriptive 论证说服力远不如 significant interaction test。在 worst tier\n      叙事中，2×2 结果最多写一段文字报告 \"no significant interaction was detected,\n      consistent with additive but not multiplicative independence\"。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-007: Error Taxonomy\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy by BCS Bins\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      对 Few-NERD exp-002 数据做系统 FP 分类（type_substitution / boundary_error /\n      false_negative / hallucination），按 BCS bin 分析差异。机械层面支撑 multi-channel\n      模型。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_overall:\n        type_substitution_pct: 0.18\n        boundary_error_pct: 0.12\n        spurious_extraction_pct: 0.45\n        missed_entity_pct: 0.25\n      type_substitution_by_bcs:\n        extreme_high_bcs_rate: 0.058\n        extreme_low_bcs_rate: 0.012\n        extreme_ratio: 4.8\n        random_high_bcs_rate: 0.022\n        random_low_bcs_rate: 0.015\n        random_ratio: 1.5\n      boundary_error_by_bcs:\n        high_bcs_rate: 0.041\n        low_bcs_rate: 0.038\n        ratio: 1.08\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n      missed_entity_by_count:\n        count_6_miss_rate: 0.28\n        count_22_miss_rate: 0.42\n        count_64_miss_rate: 0.55\n        trend: \"monotonically increasing with count\"\n      missed_entity_by_bcs:\n        high_bcs_miss_rate: 0.40\n        low_bcs_miss_rate: 0.38\n        ratio: 1.05\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n      hallucination_rate: 0.03\n      hallucination_by_bcs:\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error taxonomy 的分类本身是 noisy 的——boundary error vs type substitution 的\n      区分依赖 text_match 容差设定。在 worst tier 下：(1) type substitution 在 extreme\n      high-BCS batch 中确实更多（4.8x ratio），但 extreme batches 是刻意构造的极端\n      条件，random batches 中 ratio 仅 1.5x，实际场景中效应有限；(2) boundary error\n      不受 BCS 影响（ratio≈1.0），符合预期——boundary detection 是 span 层面的任务，\n      与 type confusability 无关；(3) missed entity（false negative）主要由 count\n      驱动（count_6 miss 28% vs count_64 miss 55%），不受 BCS 影响——支持 count→recall\n      通道；(4) 但整体 error 中 spurious extraction 占 45%，远超 type substitution\n      的 18%——这意味着 LLM 的主要问题是 \"提取不该提取的 span\" 而非 \"type 标错\"，\n      confusability 只解释了一小部分 error。worst tier 的核心问题是：type confusion\n      不是 dominant error mode，因此 confusability 的实际影响被其他 error 源稀释。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Error Distribution Overall\n        | Error Type          | Proportion | Primary Driver |\n        |---------------------|------------|----------------|\n        | Spurious Extraction | 45%        | Prompt format  |\n        | Missed Entity       | 25%        | Count (recall) |\n        | Type Substitution   | 18%        | BCS (confuse)  |\n        | Boundary Error      | 12%        | Span detection |\n      - |\n        Table: Type Substitution Rate by BCS Condition\n        | Condition     | High BCS | Low BCS | Ratio |\n        |---------------|----------|---------|-------|\n        | Extreme Batch | 0.058    | 0.012   | 4.8x  |\n        | Random Batch  | 0.022    | 0.015   | 1.5x  |\n      - |\n        Table: Missed Entity Rate by Count\n        | Count | Miss Rate | Δ vs Count_6 |\n        |-------|-----------|--------------|\n        | 6     | 0.28      | —            |\n        | 22    | 0.42      | +0.14        |\n        | 64    | 0.55      | +0.27        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Stacked bar chart of error types by BCS bin — type_substitution 在 high-BCS 中突出，但 spurious extraction 始终占主导\"\n      - \"Fig: Missed entity rate vs count — 清晰单调上升，支持 count→recall 通道\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 部分支持 multi-channel 模型：(1) type substitution 受 BCS 影响\n      （extreme 4.8x），(2) missed entity 受 count 影响（monotonic）。但 worst tier\n      下两个弱点：(a) type substitution 只占总 error 的 18%，不是 dominant mode——\n      reviewer 会质疑 \"如果 confusability 只解释 18% 的 error，实际影响有多大？\"；\n      (b) random batch ratio 仅 1.5x，远低于 extreme 的 4.8x——说明自然分布下效应\n      很小。论文只能做 descriptive analysis，不能做 formal causal claim。在 worst\n      tier 叙事中，error taxonomy 作为 supporting evidence 放在 analysis section，\n      不作为独立 finding。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-012: LLaMA Multi-Model Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复制 exp-002 protocol（Few-NERD, 25 random + extreme\n      batches, count=6/12, pairwise + per-type 分析）。检验 confusability 效应的跨模型\n      泛化性。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_f1_count64: 0.378\n      baseline_vs_qwen3: \"Δ=-3.6pp (Qwen3=0.414)\"\n      # Pairwise analysis\n      pairwise_qwen3_embed:\n        pearson_r: 0.042\n        pearson_p: 0.068\n        n_pairs: 1953\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      pairwise_qwen3_embed_nonzero:\n        spearman_rho: 0.078\n        p: 0.12\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      # Per-type analysis\n      per_type_bcs_f1:\n        spearman_rho: -0.082\n        p: 0.538\n        n_types: 58\n        partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.055\n        partial_p: 0.684\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      # Batch-level\n      batch_f1_vs_bcs:\n        count_6:\n          r: 0.108\n          p: 0.42\n        count_12:\n          r: 0.185\n          p: 0.21\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: 0.138\n          p: 0.16\n      # Confusion rate\n      confusion_rate_extreme:\n        count_6_high: 0.025\n        count_6_low: 0.010\n        ratio_6: 2.5\n        count_12_high: 0.032\n        count_12_low: 0.015\n        ratio_12: 2.1\n      confusion_rate_random:\n        count_6_ratio: 1.2\n        count_12_ratio: 1.15\n      # Comparison with Qwen3\n      cross_model_summary:\n        qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n        llama_pairwise_r: 0.042\n        qwen3_extreme_ratio: \"10-28x\"\n        llama_extreme_ratio: \"2.1-2.5x\"\n        qwen3_per_type_rho: -0.293\n        llama_per_type_rho: -0.082\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 与 Qwen3-32B 在 confusability 敏感度上存在根本差异，原因可能是：\n      (1) 模型规模差异——70B vs 32B，更大的模型有更大的 attention capacity，能更好地\n      处理 confusable types 的共现，因此 confusability 的 degradation 效应被缓解；\n      (2) instruction tuning 差异——LLaMA-3.3 的 RLHF 训练可能更强调 precision 和\n      faithfulness，模型在不确定时倾向不输出（而非猜测相似 type），导致 type confusion\n      error 本就少，confusability 信号弱；(3) internal representation 差异——LLaMA 的\n      embedding 空间对 Few-NERD types 的组织方式可能与 Qwen3 不同，Qwen3 embedding\n      中的 semantic proximity 模式不能直接迁移为 LLaMA 的 confusion 模式。\n      \n      pairwise r=0.042 (p=0.068) 在 α=0.05 下不显著但接近边界——这是最棘手的\n      结果：不能说完全无信号（p=0.068），但也不能声称显著。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      这被 reframe 为 \"confusability effects are model-dependent, with effect size\n      varying by 4x across model families (r=0.156 Qwen3 vs r=0.042 LLaMA)\"。confusion\n      rate ratio 也大幅下降（2.5x vs Qwen3 的 27.5x），进一步说明 LLaMA 对 type\n      confusion 更鲁棒。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Cross-Model Comparison (Few-NERD)\n        | Metric                    | Qwen3-32B    | LLaMA-3.3-70B | Ratio    |\n        |---------------------------|-------------|---------------|----------|\n        | Baseline F1 (count_64)    | 0.414       | 0.378         | 0.91x    |\n        | Pairwise r (Qwen3 embed)  | 0.156***    | 0.042 (ns)    | 0.27x    |\n        | Per-type ρ                | -0.293*     | -0.082 (ns)   | 0.28x    |\n        | Extreme confusion ratio   | 10-28x      | 2.1-2.5x      | 0.10x    |\n        | Random confusion ratio    | 1.7-2.4x    | 1.15-1.2x     | 0.50x    |\n      - |\n        Table: LLaMA Pairwise & Per-Type Statistics\n        | Analysis        | Statistic | Value  | p     | Verdict |\n        |-----------------|-----------|--------|-------|---------|\n        | Pairwise        | Pearson r | 0.042  | 0.068 | NS      |\n        | Pairwise NZ     | Spearman  | 0.078  | 0.120 | NS      |\n        | Per-type        | Spearman  | -0.082 | 0.538 | NS      |\n        | Per-type partial| Partial r | -0.055 | 0.684 | NS      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Side-by-side pairwise scatter (Qwen3 vs LLaMA) — Qwen3 显示清晰正相关，LLaMA 为随机散点\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-model confusion rate bar chart — Qwen3 extreme ratio 10-28x 显著高于 LLaMA 2-3x\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-type F1 vs BCS scatter (both models) — Qwen3 负斜率可见，LLaMA 平坦\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA 结果是 worst tier 中最关键的 negative result。cross_model_significant = 1\n      （仅 Qwen3），这意味着 confusability 效应可能是 Qwen3 特有的，而非 LLM IE 的\n      普遍现象。论文必须显著降级 Claim 1 的 generalizability：从 \"confusability\n      independently predicts degradation in training-free LLM IE\" 改为\n      \"confusability sensitivity varies substantially across model families, with\n      Qwen3 showing strong effects (r=0.156) and LLaMA showing weak/null effects\n      (r=0.042)\"。在 worst tier 叙事中，这可 reframe 为解释力：\"prior conflicting\n      findings about schema complexity may be partly explained by model-dependent\n      confusability sensitivity\"——将缺陷转为贡献，但 reviewer 是否买账取决于写作。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-008: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-zero：Qwen3 embedding SCS + graph coloring (τ adaptive,\n      k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches，与 single-pass 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # Graph coloring stats\n      graph_stats:\n        threshold_tau: 0.847\n        n_edges: 142\n        edge_density: 0.066\n        chromatic_number: 8\n        avg_batch_size: 8.25\n        max_batch_size: 12\n        min_batch_size: 4\n        max_intra_batch_bcs: 0.842\n      # SDGD-zero results\n      sdgd_zero:\n        f1: 0.367\n        precision: 0.318\n        recall: 0.434\n        pred_gold_ratio: 1.36\n      # Single-pass baseline (from exp003a count_64)\n      single_pass:\n        f1: 0.414\n        precision: 0.648\n        recall: 0.304\n      # Comparison\n      delta_f1_vs_single_pass: -4.7\n      delta_precision: -33.0\n      delta_recall: +13.0\n      # Per-batch breakdown\n      per_batch_f1_range: [0.28, 0.42]\n      per_batch_recall_range: [0.35, 0.52]\n      per_batch_precision_range: [0.22, 0.38]\n      # Merge statistics\n      merge_stats:\n        total_predictions: 4850\n        unique_predictions_after_dedup: 4120\n        cross_batch_span_overlap: 0.08\n        predictions_per_sample_avg: 8.2\n        gold_per_sample_avg: 5.9\n      # API cost\n      api_calls: \"8x single-pass (8000 vs 1000 for 1000 samples)\"\n      wall_clock_multiplier: 6.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 失败的核心机制是 \"disambiguation context loss\"。当 confusable types\n      被分到不同 batch 时，每个 batch 中的模型只看到 pair 的一端。例如 person-other\n      在 batch A，person-politician 在 batch B。处理含政治人物的句子时：\n      \n      - Batch A（有 person-other，无 person-politician）：模型将政治人物标为\n        person-other（因为这是最接近的可用 type）→ FP for person-other\n      - Batch B（有 person-politician，无 person-other）：模型将普通人标为\n        person-politician（同理）→ FP for person-politician\n      \n      merge 后，同一实体可能被两个 batch 分别标为不同 type（cross-batch span overlap\n      8%），评估时只有一个是 TP，另一个是 FP。更严重的是，每个 batch 只有 ~8 types，\n      模型倾向过度提取（pred/gold=1.36 vs single-pass 的 0.47），precision 从 0.648\n      暴跌到 0.318。recall 确实从 0.304 提升到 0.434（smaller batch → 更多 attention\n      给每个 type），但 precision 损失远大于 recall 增益。\n      \n      F1 = 0.367 比 single-pass 的 0.414 低 4.7pp。SDGD 的前提假设（separating\n      confusable types reduces confusion）是错误的——对 LLM 来说，看到 confusable types\n      的完整集合反而帮助 disambiguation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (Few-NERD, 66 types)\n        | Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | Pred/Gold | API Calls |\n        |-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 0.47      | 1x        |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 1.36      | 8x        |\n        | Δ           | -4.7pp| -33.0pp   | +13.0pp| +0.89     | +7x       |\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero Per-Batch Breakdown (top 4 batches)\n        | Batch | Types | Avg BCS | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n        |-------|-------|---------|-------|--------|-----------|\n        | 0     | 12    | 0.812   | 0.42  | 0.48   | 0.38      |\n        | 1     | 10    | 0.795   | 0.38  | 0.45   | 0.33      |\n        | 2     | 9     | 0.780   | 0.35  | 0.42   | 0.30      |\n        | 3     | 8     | 0.763   | 0.32  | 0.40   | 0.27      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SDGD-zero vs single-pass P/R/F1 bar chart — precision 暴跌，recall 小幅提升，net F1 下降\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-batch F1 distribution (box plot) — batch 间方差大，最差 batch F1=0.28\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-batch span overlap analysis — 8% 的 span 被多个 batch 提取为不同 type\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 的失败是 worst tier 的核心 negative result。直接否定 Claim 3。\n      failure mode 清晰且可解释：separating confusable types 剥夺了模型的 comparative\n      disambiguation 能力。这是一个 informative negative result——它揭示了 LLM IE 中\n      type co-presence 的 dual role：(1) 增加 confusability（hypothesis 的前提），\n      (2) 提供 disambiguation context（SDGD 未预见的副作用）。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      这个发现可以作为论文的一个 insight：\"confusability is a two-edged sword — the\n      same type co-presence that causes confusion also enables disambiguation\"，\n      解释为什么简单的 separation strategy 不 work。但这最多放在 Discussion section，\n      不能作为 core contribution。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-009: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN（168 event types）上的 SDGD-zero。用 adaptive threshold (k=1.0) 生成\n      confusability-minimizing batches。跨任务（NER→ED）验证 SDGD。\n    expected_results:\n      graph_stats:\n        embedding: qwen3\n        scs_mean: 0.216\n        scs_std: 0.103\n        threshold_tau: 0.319\n        n_edges: 1850\n        edge_density: 0.132\n        chromatic_number: 15\n        avg_batch_size: 11.2\n        min_batch_size: 5\n        max_batch_size: 18\n      sdgd_zero:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.168\n        exact_f1: 0.012\n        relaxed_recall: 0.130\n        relaxed_precision: 0.238\n      single_pass:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.241\n        exact_f1: 0.018\n      delta_relaxed_f1: -7.3\n      api_calls: \"15x single-pass\"\n      wall_clock_multiplier: 12.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 失败更严重（Δ=-7.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 -4.7pp），原因：\n      (1) MAVEN count curve 是上升的——更多 types 帮助模型理解 event ontology，\n      decomposition 直接损害这个优势；(2) adaptive τ=0.319（因 MAVEN Qwen3 SCS\n      分布集中在低值区间），graph 中 edge density=13.2%，coloring 产生 15 个 batch，\n      每个约 11 types——这比 single-pass 的 168 types 少了 93%的 type 上下文；\n      (3) 15 个 batch 意味着 15x API 调用，wall-clock 12.8x 但性能反而更差——\n      cost-quality 全面恶化；(4) MAVEN event trigger 是 verb/nominalization，多个\n      event type 共享同一 trigger word（如 \"attack\" 可以是 Attack 也可以是 Conflict），\n      模型需要看到完整 event taxonomy 才能正确 assign type。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (MAVEN, 168 types)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | 0.018    | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 0.012    | 15x       | 12.8x      |\n        | Δ           | -7.3pp    | -0.6pp   | +14x      | +11.8x     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SDGD-zero vs single-pass on MAVEN — 性能更差且 cost 更高，全面失败\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN batch count vs performance — 随着 batch 数量增加性能持续下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN SDGD-zero 是最差的结果之一。15x API cost 换来 -7.3pp 性能下降。\n      与 Few-NERD 的 SDGD 失败共同构成 Claim 3 的致命反证：SDGD 在两个任务上\n      都差于 single-pass，且效果 consistent（方向一致、机制相同）。在 worst tier\n      叙事中，SDGD 相关实验（exp-008, 009, 010, 011, 013, 014）全部降级为 appendix\n      中的 negative result case study，正文仅用 1-2 段文字总结 \"we also explored\n      confusability-minimizing decomposition, which failed because...\"。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-010: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-cal：用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion\n      matrix，替代 embedding SCS。与 SDGD-zero 和 single-pass 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_stats:\n        n_calibration_samples: 8\n        calibration_api_calls: 8\n        empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero: 85\n        spearman_vs_embedding_scs: 0.125\n        p_vs_embedding_scs: 0.031\n      graph_stats:\n        threshold_tau: \"adaptive on empirical confusion\"\n        n_edges: 62\n        chromatic_number: 7\n        avg_batch_size: 9.4\n      sdgd_cal:\n        f1: 0.381\n        precision: 0.342\n        recall: 0.430\n        pred_gold_ratio: 1.26\n      comparison:\n        vs_single_pass_delta: -3.3\n        vs_sdgd_zero_delta: +1.4\n        vs_random_delta: +0.7\n        vs_random_p: 0.58\n      single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.367\n      random_f1: 0.374\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 好（+1.4pp），因为 empirical confusion matrix 比 embedding\n      SCS 更准确地反映实际 model confusion：(1) 非零 confusion pair 只有 85 对（vs\n      embedding SCS 的 142 条 edge），graph 更稀疏 → 7 个 batch（vs 8 个），每个\n      batch 更大 → 更多 type 上下文；(2) calibration 捕捉到一些 embedding SCS 预测不\n      到的 confusion pattern（如语义不近但 surface form 相似的 type pair）。但 SDGD-cal\n      仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp，因为 decomposition 的核心问题（disambiguation context\n      loss）不因 confusion matrix 质量改善而消失。与 random batching 的差异仅 +0.7pp\n      (p=0.58)，不显著——confusability-aware grouping 即使用了 empirical data 也没有\n      显著优势。calibration 的额外 cost（8 次 API 调用）换来的 improvement 微乎其微。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)\n        | Method      | F1    | Δ vs SP | Precision | Recall | API Overhead   |\n        |-------------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|----------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | —       | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x             |\n        | Random (k=8)| 0.374 | -4.0    | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x             |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | -4.7    | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x             |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | -3.3    | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x + 8 calib   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Method comparison bar chart (F1) — 所有 decomposition 方法均低于 single-pass\"\n      - \"Fig: Empirical confusion vs embedding SCS scatter — 弱正相关 ρ=0.125\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 是 SDGD 方法线的 \"best effort\"——用 ground truth confusion 替代 proxy。\n      即使如此仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp。这最终否定了 confusability-minimizing\n      decomposition 的整体方法路线：问题不在 confusion matrix 的质量，而在于\n      decomposition 本身损害了 LLM 的 disambiguation context。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement over SDGD-zero 可作为 exp-015（SCS validation）\n      的间接证据：embedding proxy 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），但这\n      不是失败的主因——即使 perfect confusion matrix 也不能拯救 decomposition strategy。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-011: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN（168 types）上的 SDGD-cal：empirical confusion matrix + graph coloring。\n      Full comparison table。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_stats:\n        n_calibration_samples: 10\n        empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero: 210\n      graph_stats:\n        chromatic_number: 12\n        avg_batch_size: 14.0\n      sdgd_cal:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.188\n        exact_f1: 0.014\n      comparison:\n        vs_single_pass_delta: -5.3\n        vs_sdgd_zero_delta: +2.0\n        vs_random_delta: +0.8\n        vs_random_p: 0.62\n      single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.241\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.168\n      random_relaxed_f1: 0.180\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Few-NERD 相同模式：SDGD-cal 好于 SDGD-zero（+2.0pp）但仍远差于 single-pass\n      （-5.3pp）。MAVEN 的 empirical confusion matrix 更密（210 nonzero pairs vs\n      Few-NERD 的 85），因为 168 types 中很多 event type 确实会互相 confuse（尤其是\n      同一 FrameNet frame 下的 sibling types）。但 calibration 帮助有限——核心问题\n      仍然是 MAVEN 的性能与 type count 正相关，decomposition 损害性能。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, 168 types, relaxed matching)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP | API Calls      |\n        |-------------|-----------|---------|----------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | —       | 1x             |\n        | Random (k=12)| 0.180    | -6.1    | 12x            |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | -7.3    | 15x            |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | -5.3    | 12x + 10 calib |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN full comparison bar chart — single-pass 远超所有 decomposition 方法\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN SDGD-cal 确认 decomposition 在 event detection 上全面失败。所有方法\n      均差于 single-pass，且 MAVEN 的差距（5-7pp）比 Few-NERD（3-5pp）更大。\n      这强化了 worst tier 的核心结论：decomposition 不是通用 solution，type co-presence\n      在很多场景中是 feature 而非 bug。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-013: Random Batching Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      与 SDGD-zero 相同 batch 数量 k，随机分组。隔离 confusability-aware grouping\n      的价值（排除 batch count reduction 的贡献）。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd:\n        random_f1: 0.374\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.367\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: -0.7\n        paired_t_p: 0.68\n        n_random_seeds: 10\n        random_f1_std: 0.018\n        random_f1_range: [0.348, 0.402]\n        single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      maven:\n        random_relaxed_f1: 0.180\n        sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.168\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: -1.2\n        paired_t_p: 0.42\n        n_random_seeds: 5\n      interpretation:\n        sdgd_vs_random_significant: false\n        confusability_aware_grouping_benefit: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching 在 10 个 random seeds 上平均 F1=0.374（std=0.018），而 SDGD-zero\n      F1=0.367。SDGD 比 random 差 0.7pp（p=0.68），差异不显著。实际上 SDGD 可能略\n      差于 random，因为 SDGD 刻意将 confusable types 分开——这意味着每个 batch 内的\n      types 都是 semantically distant 的，模型缺乏同一 semantic cluster 的 types\n      作为 disambiguation anchor。Random batching 偶尔会把 confusable types 放在一起\n      （概率约 1/k），这些 batch 的 disambiguation 更好，平均下来 random 反而略优。\n      \n      在 MAVEN 上同样：random F1=0.180 vs SDGD F1=0.168（Δ=-1.2pp, p=0.42）。\n      SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不仅无益，可能有害。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (Few-NERD, k=8)\n        | Method     | Mean F1 | Std   | Range         | vs Single-Pass |\n        |------------|---------|-------|---------------|----------------|\n        | Random×10  | 0.374   | 0.018 | [0.348,0.402] | -4.0pp         |\n        | SDGD-zero  | 0.367   | —     | —             | -4.7pp         |\n        | Δ (SDGD-Random) | -0.7pp | — | —           | p=0.68 (NS)    |\n      - |\n        Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (MAVEN, k=15/12)\n        | Method     | Relaxed F1 | vs Single-Pass |\n        |------------|-----------|----------------|\n        | Random×5   | 0.180     | -6.1pp         |\n        | SDGD-zero  | 0.168     | -7.3pp         |\n        | Δ          | -1.2pp    | p=0.42 (NS)    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Random batching F1 distribution (violin plot, 10 seeds) with SDGD-zero point overlaid — SDGD 在 random 的分布内\"\n      - \"Fig: Paired comparison scatter (random seed F1 vs SDGD F1) — 大多数 random seed 优于 SDGD\"\n    analysis: >\n      Random batching ablation 是 Claim 3 的 definitive kill shot。SDGD 不显著优于\n      random→confusability-aware grouping 无价值。combined with SDGD < single-pass→\n      decomposition 本身有害。Claim 3 完全不成立。在 worst tier 叙事中，这个实验\n      的 negative result 本身有教育意义：it demonstrates that the intuitive principle\n      \"separate confusable types\" is wrong for LLM IE，因为 LLMs 使用 type co-presence\n      做 comparative reasoning。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-014: Per-Type Splitting Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      1 type per batch（k=66/168）。Decomposition 的上界。揭示 latency-quality tradeoff。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd:\n        per_type_f1: 0.330\n        per_type_precision: 0.225\n        per_type_recall: 0.620\n        api_calls: \"66x single-pass\"\n        wall_clock_multiplier: 48.0\n      maven:\n        per_type_relaxed_f1: 0.108\n        api_calls: \"168x single-pass\"\n        wall_clock_multiplier: 135.0\n      comparison_fewnerd:\n        single_pass: 0.414\n        sdgd_zero: 0.367\n        random: 0.374\n        per_type: 0.330\n      ordering: \"single-pass > random ≈ SDGD-zero > per-type\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 是 decomposition 的极端形式：每个 batch 只有 1 个 type。\n      这完全消除 type confusion（BCS=0），但也完全消除 disambiguation context。\n      \n      Few-NERD 结果（F1=0.330）几乎等于 exp003a count_1 的 F1=0.323——符合预期，\n      因为 per-type extraction 本质就是 count=1。precision 极低（0.225）因为模型\n      只知道一个 type，会把任何像样的 span 都标为该 type（massive over-extraction）。\n      recall 最高（0.620）因为模型 aggressively 搜索这个 type 的所有 instance。\n      \n      MAVEN 更惨（relaxed F1=0.108），因为 MAVEN 的 count_1 relaxed_F1 就只有 0.098。\n      168x API 调用使 wall-clock time 完全不可接受。\n      \n      排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 证明：decomposition granularity\n      与性能成反比。batch 越大越好（更多 type context），单pass 最优。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Full Method Comparison (Few-NERD)\n        | Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x        | 5.5x       |\n        | Random (k=8)| 0.374 | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\n        | Per-type    | 0.330 | 0.225     | 0.620  | 66x       | 48x        |\n      - |\n        Table: Full Method Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-----------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | 12x       | 10x        |\n        | Random      | 0.180     | 12x       | 10x        |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 15x       | 12.8x      |\n        | Per-type    | 0.108     | 168x      | 135x       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 vs API cost Pareto frontier — single-pass 是 Pareto optimal，所有 decomposition 方法 dominated\"\n      - \"Fig: Precision-Recall tradeoff by method — decomposition 方法在 high-recall low-precision 角落\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type ablation 完成了 decomposition failure 的完整图景。方法排序\n      single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 说明：(1) decomposition granularity\n      与 F1 反相关；(2) type co-presence 是 net positive（disambiguation > confusion）；\n      (3) SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不提供额外价值（≈ random）。\n      在 worst tier 叙事中，这个结果可 reframe 为 empirical finding：\"LLM IE\n      benefits from full schema visibility; type co-presence enables comparative\n      reasoning that outweighs confusability-induced errors\"——这本身是一个有价值\n      的 insight，但不是 method contribution。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-015: SCS Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Embedding SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      计算 embedding SCS（Qwen3 / MiniLM）与 empirical confusion matrix 之间的\n      rank correlation。验证 embedding proxy 对实际 model confusion 的预测力。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.125\n        p: 0.031\n        kendall_tau: 0.092\n        p_kendall: 0.044\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 85\n      minilm_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.098\n        p: 0.082\n        kendall_tau: 0.071\n        p_kendall: 0.115\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 85\n      top_confused_pair_scs_rank:\n        person_other_politician:\n          scs_rank: 3\n          confusion_rank: 1\n        building_other_library:\n          scs_rank: 45\n          confusion_rank: 8\n          comment: \"high confusion, low SCS — embedding 未捕捉的 confusion pattern\"\n      scs_false_positive_rate: 0.42\n      scs_false_negative_rate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），原因：(1) embedding\n      similarity 反映 semantic proximity，但 model confusion 还受 surface form\n      similarity、type definition wording、in-context position 等因素影响——这些因素\n      与 embedding space 正交；(2) SCS 是对称的（sim(A,B)=sim(B,A)），但实际 confusion\n      是非对称的（person-other → person-politician 的概率可能远高于反向）；(3) 42%\n      的 false positive rate 意味着 SCS 预测为 confusable 的 type pair 中近一半实际\n      不被 confuse——这些 false alarm 导致 SDGD-zero 过度分离 types，graph 变密，\n      batch 数量过多。\n      \n      MiniLM SCS 更差（ρ=0.098, p=0.082），因为 MiniLM 是 general-purpose sentence\n      embedding，不 align 到 Qwen3 的 internal representation。这解释了为什么\n      extraction model alignment 对 per-type signal 很重要（exp-002 中 Qwen3 per-type\n      ρ=-0.293 vs MiniLM ρ≈0）。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\n        | Embedding | Spearman ρ | p     | Kendall τ | p     |\n        |-----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------|\n        | Qwen3     | 0.125     | 0.031 | 0.092     | 0.044 |\n        | MiniLM    | 0.098     | 0.082 | 0.071     | 0.115 |\n      - |\n        Table: SCS Proxy Error Analysis\n        | Metric              | Qwen3 | MiniLM |\n        |---------------------|-------|--------|\n        | False Positive Rate | 0.42  | 0.48   |\n        | False Negative Rate | 0.35  | 0.40   |\n        | Top-1 Match         | Yes   | No     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (Qwen3) — 弱正相关，大量 off-diagonal noise\"\n      - \"Fig: Confusion asymmetry heatmap — 展示 confusion matrix 的非对称性，SCS 无法捕捉\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS validation 结果解释了 SDGD 失败的一个次要原因（proxy 质量差），但不是主因\n      （主因是 decomposition 本身有害）。ρ=0.125 说明 embedding SCS 只能解释 ~1.6%\n      的 confusion variance——作为 graph 构建的基础远远不够。即使用 empirical confusion\n      (exp-010 SDGD-cal) 也只比 random 好 0.7pp（不显著），所以 proxy 质量不是瓶颈。\n      在 worst tier 叙事中，SCS validation 作为 methodological finding 报告：\n      \"embedding-based confusability proxies have limited predictive power for actual\n      model confusion patterns, suggesting that confusability is mediated by factors\n      beyond semantic similarity\"——这对未来工作有指导价值。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # Summary tables for paper\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Cross-Experiment Summary (for paper narrative)\"\n    plan_id: \"summary\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有实验的 worst tier 结果，构建论文核心 tables 和 narrative。\n    expected_results:\n      # Claim 1 summary\n      claim1_pairwise_matrix:\n        qwen3_fewnerd: \"r=0.156*** ✓\"\n        qwen3_maven: \"r=-0.009 (ns) ✗\"\n        qwen3_fewrel: \"pending\"\n        minilm_fewnerd: \"not tested\"\n        minilm_maven: \"r=0.115*** ✓\"\n        minilm_fewrel: \"Δ=21-50pp ✓ (pilot)\"\n        llama_fewnerd: \"r=0.042 (ns) ✗\"\n        significant_cells: 3\n        total_cells: 7\n        verdict: \"partial — 3/7 significant, no single embedding/model universally works\"\n      # Claim 2 summary\n      claim2_evidence:\n        count_recall_monotonic: true\n        bcs_type_substitution_ratio_extreme: \"4.8x\"\n        bcs_type_substitution_ratio_random: \"1.5x\"\n        interaction_significant: false\n        error_taxonomy_dominant_mode: \"spurious extraction (45%), not type confusion (18%)\"\n        verdict: \"directional — channels exist but confusability channel is weak relative to other error sources\"\n      # Claim 3 summary\n      claim3_evidence:\n        sdgd_zero_fewnerd: \"F1=0.367, Δ=-4.7pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_zero_maven: \"relF1=0.168, Δ=-7.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_cal_fewnerd: \"F1=0.381, Δ=-3.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_cal_maven: \"relF1=0.188, Δ=-5.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_vs_random_significant: false\n        per_type_worst: true\n        verdict: \"FAILED — all decomposition methods inferior to single-pass\"\n      # Paper structure\n      recommended_paper_structure:\n        - \"1. Introduction: 'What makes schemas complex for LLMs?'\"\n        - \"2. Related Work: decomposition approaches + empirical studies\"\n        - \"3. Experimental Setup: 3 tasks, 2 models, 2 embeddings\"\n        - \"4. Finding 1: Pairwise confusability predicts type confusion (model-dependent)\"\n        - \"5. Finding 2: Count and confusability act through distinguishable channels\"\n        - \"6. Finding 3: Per-type aggregation introduces centrality confound\"\n        - \"7. Finding 4: Confusability-minimizing decomposition fails (negative result)\"\n        - \"8. Discussion: implications for future work\"\n        - \"9. Conclusion\"\n      recommended_venue: \"EMNLP 2026 Findings (realistic), Main (stretch)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst tier 总体图景：论文有两个可靠发现（pairwise confusability signal on\n      Qwen3×FewNERD + MiniLM×MAVEN；centrality confound on MAVEN）和一系列 informative\n      negative results（LLaMA 无信号、SDGD 全面失败、interaction 不显著）。叙事必须\n      从 \"we discover and exploit confusability\" 彻底转为 \"we systematically investigate\n      schema complexity, finding that confusability effects are real but model-dependent,\n      and that the intuitive decomposition strategy fails because LLMs need type\n      co-presence for disambiguation\"。这种 \"honest empirical study with negative\n      results\" 的论文在 EMNLP Findings 有先例（如 \"Do Prompt-Based Models Really\n      Understand the Meaning of Their Prompts?\" ACL 2022），但需要极强的写作功力\n      和清晰的 takeaway。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Pairwise SCS-Confusion Signal (Cross-Task × Cross-Model × Cross-Embedding)\n        | Model  | Embedding | Few-NERD (NER) | MAVEN (ED) | FewRel (RE) |\n        |--------|-----------|----------------|------------|-------------|\n        | Qwen3  | Qwen3     | r=0.156***     | r=-0.009   | —           |\n        | Qwen3  | MiniLM    | —              | r=0.115*** | Δ=21-50pp*  |\n        | LLaMA  | Qwen3     | r=0.042        | —          | —           |\n        *** p<0.001, * pilot only\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD Full Comparison (worst tier)\n        | Method       | Few-NERD F1 | Δ vs SP | MAVEN relF1 | Δ vs SP |\n        |-------------|-------------|---------|-------------|---------|\n        | Single-pass  | 0.414       | —       | 0.241       | —       |\n        | SDGD-cal     | 0.381       | -3.3    | 0.188       | -5.3    |\n        | Random (=k)  | 0.374       | -4.0    | 0.180       | -6.1    |\n        | SDGD-zero    | 0.367       | -4.7    | 0.168       | -7.3    |\n        | Per-type     | 0.330       | -8.4    | 0.108       | -13.3   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 论文 hero figure — schema complexity 的 multi-dimensional decomposition (count × confusability × model)，展示不同维度的 effect 和 interaction\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-experiment evidence summary — 3×3 grid 展示 task × model × embedding 的 signal 有无\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 论文的核心卖点不是 positive findings 而是 systematic methodology\n      和 honest reporting。三个 takeaway：(1) confusability 信号存在但\n      model/embedding-dependent——未来工作不能假设 universal confusability measure；\n      (2) per-type 聚合有 centrality confound——未来工作应使用 pairwise 分析；\n      (3) confusability-minimizing decomposition 失败——LLM 需要 type co-presence\n      做 comparative reasoning，简单分离策略适得其反。这些 negative-but-informative\n      results 加上 controlled experimental design 可以支撑一篇 Findings paper。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14331,"cache_read_input_tokens":43817,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6066cd7-3b7c-4597-bdab-f4c39ace5902","uuid":"e583ca40-cdde-48f0-a7f2-318ccf9026c9"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":745897,"duration_api_ms":747554,"num_turns":5,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  完全放弃 SDGD 方法贡献。论文 reframe 为纯系统性实证分析：首次控制实验揭示\n  schema complexity 不是一维问题——count 和 confusability 通过正交通道降低性能，\n  但 confusability 信号高度依赖模型和 embedding 选择。pairwise confusability 是\n  比 per-type 聚合更鲁棒的度量，但仅在特定 model×embedding×schema 组合下显著。\n  centrality confound 发现本身是方法论贡献。模型特异性（Qwen3 vs LLaMA）reframe\n  为 \"confusability effects are model-dependent\"——将弱点转为解释力。论文结构改为\n  \"question→controlled experiments→findings→implications\"。EMNLP Findings 是现实\n  预期，Main 可冲但 acceptance variance 大。SDGD 降为 appendix 中的 negative result\n  case study，正文不再作为核心贡献。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-004: MAVEN 全量 confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"MAVEN Full Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN Event Detection（168 event types, FrameNet hierarchy）的完整 confusability\n      研究：500-sample 重跑 count curve + within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise/per-type\n      双 embedding 分析 + confusion rate 分析。核心跨任务（NER→ED）验证。\n    expected_results:\n      # Count curve (500 samples, V2 prompt, relaxed matching)\n      count_curve_relaxed_f1:\n        count_1: 0.098\n        count_6: 0.112\n        count_12: 0.155\n        count_22: 0.192\n        count_44: 0.238\n        count_64: 0.241\n        count_100: 0.243\n      count_curve_exact_f1:\n        count_1: 0.008\n        count_6: 0.005\n        count_12: 0.011\n        count_22: 0.016\n        count_44: 0.021\n        count_64: 0.018\n      count_curve_recall_trend: \"monotonically increasing 0.07→0.19 (opposite of Few-NERD)\"\n      count_curve_precision_trend: \"roughly flat 0.15-0.40, noisy\"\n      # Within-count BCS-relaxed_F1 correlation (key new analysis)\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_6:\n          r: 0.175\n          p: 0.185\n          n: 27\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n        count_12:\n          r: 0.124\n          p: 0.315\n          n: 27\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: 0.142\n          p: 0.108\n          n: 54\n          direction: positive\n          verdict: FAIL\n      # Pairwise SCS-confusion (reconfirmation with 500 samples)\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: -0.009\n        pearson_p: 0.38\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.115\n        pearson_p: 2.1e-42\n        n_pairs: 14028\n        spearman_rho: 0.128\n        nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.185\n        verdict: PASS\n      # Per-type analysis (reconfirmation)\n      per_type_qwen3:\n        spearman_rho: 0.195\n        p: 0.018\n        direction: positive_confounded\n      per_type_minilm:\n        spearman_rho: 0.212\n        p: 0.009\n        direction: positive_confounded\n      # Confusion rate ratios\n      confusion_rate_extreme:\n        count_6_ratio: 5.8\n        count_12_ratio: 4.2\n      confusion_rate_random:\n        count_6_ratio: 1.4\n        count_12_ratio: 1.3\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 的 168 event types 全部来自 FrameNet，同一语义域，导致 type embedding\n      分布高度同质。这造成三个后果：(1) count curve 反转——更多 types 为模型提供更\n      丰富的 event ontology 上下文，帮助模型理解每个 type 在 taxonomy 中的位置，因此\n      F1 随 count 增加而上升；(2) within-count BCS 相关为正方向——高 BCS batch 包含\n      语义中心的常见 event types（如 Killing, Attack, Movement），这些 types 在\n      training data 中频次高、定义清晰，LLM 本就擅长提取，因此高 BCS → 高 F1，\n      这是 centrality confound 而非 confusability 效应；(3) confusion rate 比\n      Few-NERD 低得多（5.8x vs 27.5x），因为 event trigger 本身是 verb/nominalization\n      而非 entity mention，type confusion 的表现形式不同（trigger 共享率高但不一定是\n      confusability 导致）。pairwise MiniLM 仍显著（r=0.115, p≈0），因为 n=14028 pair\n      提供了极大统计功效，即使效应量小也能检出——但这个 r 值比 Few-NERD 的 0.156 低，\n      且 Qwen3 pairwise 完全不显著，说明 pairwise 信号在同质 schema 上高度依赖\n      embedding 选择。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Count Curve (500 samples, relaxed matching)\n        | Count | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | Recall | Precision | Pred/Gold |\n        |-------|-----------|----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n        | 1     | 0.098     | 0.008    | 0.070  | 0.162     | 0.43      |\n        | 6     | 0.112     | 0.005    | 0.085  | 0.165     | 0.52      |\n        | 12    | 0.155     | 0.011    | 0.118  | 0.226     | 0.52      |\n        | 22    | 0.192     | 0.016    | 0.148  | 0.274     | 0.54      |\n        | 44    | 0.238     | 0.021    | 0.180  | 0.350     | 0.51      |\n        | 64    | 0.241     | 0.018    | 0.182  | 0.358     | 0.51      |\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Within-Count BCS-F1 Correlation\n        | Count | r     | p     | Direction | Verdict |\n        |-------|-------|-------|-----------|---------|\n        | 6     | +0.175| 0.185 | positive  | FAIL    |\n        | 12    | +0.124| 0.315 | positive  | FAIL    |\n        | Pooled| +0.142| 0.108 | positive  | FAIL    |\n      - |\n        Table: MAVEN Pairwise & Per-Type (2×2 embedding matrix)\n        |          | Pairwise r (p)         | Per-type ρ (p)       |\n        |----------|------------------------|----------------------|\n        | Qwen3    | -0.009 (0.38) ✗        | +0.195 (0.018) ✗     |\n        | MiniLM   | +0.115 (2.1e-42) ✓     | +0.212 (0.009) ✗     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN count curve (relaxed F1 vs type count) — 上升趋势，与 Few-NERD 相反\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN pairwise scatter (MiniLM SCS vs confusion count) — 弱正相关 r=0.115，点云密集在低相似度区域\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN per-type scatter (mean BCS vs F1) — 正方向，标注 centrality confound interpretation\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN 结果确认 centrality confound 假说：在语义同质 schema 中，per-type 和\n      within-count batch-level 分析均被 confound。唯一存活的信号是 MiniLM pairwise\n      (r=0.115)，但 Qwen3 pairwise 失败，且效应量小（r²=1.3%）。MAVEN 的 count curve\n      反转是对 SDGD 方法的致命打击——如果更多 types 在 prompt 中反而帮助模型，那么\n      decomposition（减少 types）必然降低性能。worst tier 叙事中，MAVEN 作为\n      \"centrality confound case study\" 仍有方法论价值，但不支持 SDGD 的前提假设。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-005: DocRED confusability 研究\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"DocRED Confusability Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      DocRED（96 relation types）上的 confusability 研究：count curve + BCS 相关分析。\n      文档级 RE 的 scaling stress test。\n    expected_results:\n      count_curve_f1:\n        count_4: 0.185\n        count_8: 0.192\n        count_16: 0.198\n        count_32: 0.203\n        count_48: 0.208\n        count_96: 0.195\n      count_curve_trend: \"near-flat with slight peak at count_48, no clear monotonic pattern\"\n      within_count_bcs_f1:\n        count_8:\n          r: 0.032\n          p: 0.62\n          verdict: FAIL\n        count_16:\n          r: -0.058\n          p: 0.48\n          verdict: FAIL\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: -0.015\n          p: 0.84\n          verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_qwen3:\n        pearson_r: 0.023\n        pearson_p: 0.14\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        verdict: FAIL\n      pairwise_minilm:\n        pearson_r: 0.031\n        pearson_p: 0.08\n        n_pairs: 4560\n        verdict: FAIL\n      per_type_bcs_f1:\n        spearman_rho: -0.04\n        p: 0.72\n        verdict: FAIL\n      confusion_rate_extreme_ratio: 1.8\n      overall_baseline_f1: 0.195\n    result_rationale: >\n      DocRED 是文档级 RE，每个样本包含多个句子和多个 entity pairs。性能瓶颈完全不在\n      type confusability 上，而在于：(1) 跨句推理能力——关系证据分散在多个句子中，LLM\n      需要 coreference 和 multi-hop reasoning；(2) entity pair 组合爆炸——文档中 n\n      个实体产生 O(n²) 个候选关系对，模型必须处理大量负样本；(3) 关系类型定义本身\n      依赖 entity type 约束（如 \"place_of_birth\" 要求 subject=person, object=location），\n      这种结构化约束比 embedding 相似度更能预测性能。confusability 信号被这些更强的\n      因素完全淹没。count curve 近乎平坦，因为文档级 RE 的 prompt 长度主要由文档内容\n      （而非 type 定义）决定——96 个 relation type name 只占 prompt 的很小比例。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: DocRED Count Curve (document-level RE)\n        | Count | F1    | Recall | Precision | Confusion Rate |\n        |-------|-------|--------|-----------|---------------|\n        | 4     | 0.185 | 0.145  | 0.256     | 0.008         |\n        | 8     | 0.192 | 0.152  | 0.261     | 0.012         |\n        | 16    | 0.198 | 0.158  | 0.264     | 0.015         |\n        | 32    | 0.203 | 0.165  | 0.258     | 0.018         |\n        | 48    | 0.208 | 0.170  | 0.261     | 0.019         |\n        | 96    | 0.195 | 0.160  | 0.250     | 0.022         |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DocRED count curve — near-flat, 与 Few-NERD/MAVEN 的明显趋势形成对比\"\n      - \"Fig: DocRED within-count BCS scatter — 无相关，点云随机分布\"\n    analysis: >\n      DocRED 结果是完全的 null result。confusability 假说在文档级 RE 上完全不成立。\n      worst tier 叙事中，DocRED 证明 confusability 效应受限于 sentence-level 任务——\n      文档级任务中其他复杂度维度（跨句推理、entity pair 组合）占主导。如果论文要报告\n      此结果，需要 reframe 为 \"boundary condition\"：confusability 效应在 type\n      definitions 占 prompt 显著比例的任务中才成立。但此实验为 P1，worst tier 下可能\n      不运行（10 天内优先 P0 实验），视为 supplementary material。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-006: 2×2 Interaction Effect\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Count × Confusability Interaction Effect\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上 {low count=6, high count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} 的 2×2 因子设计。\n      检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应（additive vs multiplicative）。\n    expected_results:\n      cell_means_f1:\n        low_count_low_bcs: 0.348\n        low_count_high_bcs: 0.312\n        high_count_low_bcs: 0.298\n        high_count_high_bcs: 0.255\n      two_way_anova:\n        count_main_effect:\n          F: 7.82\n          p: 0.008\n          eta_sq: 0.14\n          verdict: SIGNIFICANT\n        bcs_main_effect:\n          F: 2.93\n          p: 0.094\n          eta_sq: 0.06\n          verdict: MARGINAL\n        interaction:\n          F: 0.31\n          p: 0.582\n          eta_sq: 0.006\n          verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      n_batches_per_cell: 12\n      total_n: 48\n      simple_effects:\n        bcs_at_low_count:\n          delta_f1: -0.036\n          p: 0.22\n        bcs_at_high_count:\n          delta_f1: -0.043\n          p: 0.18\n    result_rationale: >\n      2×2 设计的统计功效受限：每个 cell 约 12 个 batch，总 n=48。在这个样本量下，\n      检测交互效应需要 η²≥0.10 的大效应量。实际中，count 的主效应最强（η²=0.14），\n      因为 count 直接影响 prompt 长度和 attention 分配，信号最清晰。BCS 主效应仅为\n      marginal（p=0.094），因为 batch-level BCS 与 F1 的关系本就受到 type frequency\n      distribution 等 confound 的干扰——exp-002 已经表明 batch-level 信号远弱于\n      pairwise-level。交互效应完全不显著（p=0.582），说明 count 和 confusability 的\n      联合效应是（弱）加性的，不存在 multiplicative synergy。这在 worst tier 中意味\n      着论文只能声称 \"两个通道可能独立\" 但无法用 formal interaction test 支撑。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: 2×2 Cell Means (F1, text_match)\n        |                | Low BCS     | High BCS    | BCS Effect |\n        |----------------|-------------|-------------|------------|\n        | Low Count (6)  | 0.348       | 0.312       | Δ=-0.036   |\n        | High Count (22)| 0.298       | 0.255       | Δ=-0.043   |\n        | Count Effect   | Δ=-0.050   | Δ=-0.057   |            |\n      - |\n        Table: Two-Way ANOVA Results\n        | Source       | F     | p     | η²    | Verdict     |\n        |-------------|-------|-------|-------|-------------|\n        | Count        | 7.82  | 0.008 | 0.14  | Significant |\n        | BCS          | 2.93  | 0.094 | 0.06  | Marginal    |\n        | Count × BCS  | 0.31  | 0.582 | 0.006 | NS          |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 2×2 interaction plot (F1 vs count, separate lines for low/high BCS) — 近似平行线，无交互\"\n      - \"Fig: Cell means bar chart with error bars — BCS 差异在两个 count level 上方向一致但均不显著\"\n    analysis: >\n      交互效应不显著是 worst tier 对 Claim 2（multi-channel degradation）的重大打击。\n      论文无法用 formal factorial design 证明两通道正交。只能退而求其次，基于 error\n      taxonomy（exp-007）做 descriptive argument：count 降低 recall（omission），\n      confusability 增加 type confusion（substitution），两类错误机制不同→暗示正交。\n      但这种 descriptive 论证说服力远不如 significant interaction test。在 worst tier\n      叙事中，2×2 结果最多写一段文字报告 \"no significant interaction was detected,\n      consistent with additive but not multiplicative independence\"。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-007: Error Taxonomy\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Systematic Error Taxonomy by BCS Bins\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      对 Few-NERD exp-002 数据做系统 FP 分类（type_substitution / boundary_error /\n      false_negative / hallucination），按 BCS bin 分析差异。机械层面支撑 multi-channel\n      模型。\n    expected_results:\n      error_distribution_overall:\n        type_substitution_pct: 0.18\n        boundary_error_pct: 0.12\n        spurious_extraction_pct: 0.45\n        missed_entity_pct: 0.25\n      type_substitution_by_bcs:\n        extreme_high_bcs_rate: 0.058\n        extreme_low_bcs_rate: 0.012\n        extreme_ratio: 4.8\n        random_high_bcs_rate: 0.022\n        random_low_bcs_rate: 0.015\n        random_ratio: 1.5\n      boundary_error_by_bcs:\n        high_bcs_rate: 0.041\n        low_bcs_rate: 0.038\n        ratio: 1.08\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n      missed_entity_by_count:\n        count_6_miss_rate: 0.28\n        count_22_miss_rate: 0.42\n        count_64_miss_rate: 0.55\n        trend: \"monotonically increasing with count\"\n      missed_entity_by_bcs:\n        high_bcs_miss_rate: 0.40\n        low_bcs_miss_rate: 0.38\n        ratio: 1.05\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n      hallucination_rate: 0.03\n      hallucination_by_bcs:\n        verdict: NO_EFFECT\n    result_rationale: >\n      Error taxonomy 的分类本身是 noisy 的——boundary error vs type substitution 的\n      区分依赖 text_match 容差设定。在 worst tier 下：(1) type substitution 在 extreme\n      high-BCS batch 中确实更多（4.8x ratio），但 extreme batches 是刻意构造的极端\n      条件，random batches 中 ratio 仅 1.5x，实际场景中效应有限；(2) boundary error\n      不受 BCS 影响（ratio≈1.0），符合预期——boundary detection 是 span 层面的任务，\n      与 type confusability 无关；(3) missed entity（false negative）主要由 count\n      驱动（count_6 miss 28% vs count_64 miss 55%），不受 BCS 影响——支持 count→recall\n      通道；(4) 但整体 error 中 spurious extraction 占 45%，远超 type substitution\n      的 18%——这意味着 LLM 的主要问题是 \"提取不该提取的 span\" 而非 \"type 标错\"，\n      confusability 只解释了一小部分 error。worst tier 的核心问题是：type confusion\n      不是 dominant error mode，因此 confusability 的实际影响被其他 error 源稀释。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Error Distribution Overall\n        | Error Type          | Proportion | Primary Driver |\n        |---------------------|------------|----------------|\n        | Spurious Extraction | 45%        | Prompt format  |\n        | Missed Entity       | 25%        | Count (recall) |\n        | Type Substitution   | 18%        | BCS (confuse)  |\n        | Boundary Error      | 12%        | Span detection |\n      - |\n        Table: Type Substitution Rate by BCS Condition\n        | Condition     | High BCS | Low BCS | Ratio |\n        |---------------|----------|---------|-------|\n        | Extreme Batch | 0.058    | 0.012   | 4.8x  |\n        | Random Batch  | 0.022    | 0.015   | 1.5x  |\n      - |\n        Table: Missed Entity Rate by Count\n        | Count | Miss Rate | Δ vs Count_6 |\n        |-------|-----------|--------------|\n        | 6     | 0.28      | —            |\n        | 22    | 0.42      | +0.14        |\n        | 64    | 0.55      | +0.27        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Stacked bar chart of error types by BCS bin — type_substitution 在 high-BCS 中突出，但 spurious extraction 始终占主导\"\n      - \"Fig: Missed entity rate vs count — 清晰单调上升，支持 count→recall 通道\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error taxonomy 部分支持 multi-channel 模型：(1) type substitution 受 BCS 影响\n      （extreme 4.8x），(2) missed entity 受 count 影响（monotonic）。但 worst tier\n      下两个弱点：(a) type substitution 只占总 error 的 18%，不是 dominant mode——\n      reviewer 会质疑 \"如果 confusability 只解释 18% 的 error，实际影响有多大？\"；\n      (b) random batch ratio 仅 1.5x，远低于 extreme 的 4.8x——说明自然分布下效应\n      很小。论文只能做 descriptive analysis，不能做 formal causal claim。在 worst\n      tier 叙事中，error taxonomy 作为 supporting evidence 放在 analysis section，\n      不作为独立 finding。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-012: LLaMA Multi-Model Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.3-70B Multi-Model Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复制 exp-002 protocol（Few-NERD, 25 random + extreme\n      batches, count=6/12, pairwise + per-type 分析）。检验 confusability 效应的跨模型\n      泛化性。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_f1_count64: 0.378\n      baseline_vs_qwen3: \"Δ=-3.6pp (Qwen3=0.414)\"\n      # Pairwise analysis\n      pairwise_qwen3_embed:\n        pearson_r: 0.042\n        pearson_p: 0.068\n        n_pairs: 1953\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      pairwise_qwen3_embed_nonzero:\n        spearman_rho: 0.078\n        p: 0.12\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      # Per-type analysis\n      per_type_bcs_f1:\n        spearman_rho: -0.082\n        p: 0.538\n        n_types: 58\n        partial_r_ctrl_logfreq: -0.055\n        partial_p: 0.684\n        verdict: NOT_SIGNIFICANT\n      # Batch-level\n      batch_f1_vs_bcs:\n        count_6:\n          r: 0.108\n          p: 0.42\n        count_12:\n          r: 0.185\n          p: 0.21\n        partial_pooled:\n          r: 0.138\n          p: 0.16\n      # Confusion rate\n      confusion_rate_extreme:\n        count_6_high: 0.025\n        count_6_low: 0.010\n        ratio_6: 2.5\n        count_12_high: 0.032\n        count_12_low: 0.015\n        ratio_12: 2.1\n      confusion_rate_random:\n        count_6_ratio: 1.2\n        count_12_ratio: 1.15\n      # Comparison with Qwen3\n      cross_model_summary:\n        qwen3_pairwise_r: 0.156\n        llama_pairwise_r: 0.042\n        qwen3_extreme_ratio: \"10-28x\"\n        llama_extreme_ratio: \"2.1-2.5x\"\n        qwen3_per_type_rho: -0.293\n        llama_per_type_rho: -0.082\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLaMA-3.3-70B 与 Qwen3-32B 在 confusability 敏感度上存在根本差异，原因可能是：\n      (1) 模型规模差异——70B vs 32B，更大的模型有更大的 attention capacity，能更好地\n      处理 confusable types 的共现，因此 confusability 的 degradation 效应被缓解；\n      (2) instruction tuning 差异——LLaMA-3.3 的 RLHF 训练可能更强调 precision 和\n      faithfulness，模型在不确定时倾向不输出（而非猜测相似 type），导致 type confusion\n      error 本就少，confusability 信号弱；(3) internal representation 差异——LLaMA 的\n      embedding 空间对 Few-NERD types 的组织方式可能与 Qwen3 不同，Qwen3 embedding\n      中的 semantic proximity 模式不能直接迁移为 LLaMA 的 confusion 模式。\n      \n      pairwise r=0.042 (p=0.068) 在 α=0.05 下不显著但接近边界——这是最棘手的\n      结果：不能说完全无信号（p=0.068），但也不能声称显著。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      这被 reframe 为 \"confusability effects are model-dependent, with effect size\n      varying by 4x across model families (r=0.156 Qwen3 vs r=0.042 LLaMA)\"。confusion\n      rate ratio 也大幅下降（2.5x vs Qwen3 的 27.5x），进一步说明 LLaMA 对 type\n      confusion 更鲁棒。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Cross-Model Comparison (Few-NERD)\n        | Metric                    | Qwen3-32B    | LLaMA-3.3-70B | Ratio    |\n        |---------------------------|-------------|---------------|----------|\n        | Baseline F1 (count_64)    | 0.414       | 0.378         | 0.91x    |\n        | Pairwise r (Qwen3 embed)  | 0.156***    | 0.042 (ns)    | 0.27x    |\n        | Per-type ρ                | -0.293*     | -0.082 (ns)   | 0.28x    |\n        | Extreme confusion ratio   | 10-28x      | 2.1-2.5x      | 0.10x    |\n        | Random confusion ratio    | 1.7-2.4x    | 1.15-1.2x     | 0.50x    |\n      - |\n        Table: LLaMA Pairwise & Per-Type Statistics\n        | Analysis        | Statistic | Value  | p     | Verdict |\n        |-----------------|-----------|--------|-------|---------|\n        | Pairwise        | Pearson r | 0.042  | 0.068 | NS      |\n        | Pairwise NZ     | Spearman  | 0.078  | 0.120 | NS      |\n        | Per-type        | Spearman  | -0.082 | 0.538 | NS      |\n        | Per-type partial| Partial r | -0.055 | 0.684 | NS      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Side-by-side pairwise scatter (Qwen3 vs LLaMA) — Qwen3 显示清晰正相关，LLaMA 为随机散点\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-model confusion rate bar chart — Qwen3 extreme ratio 10-28x 显著高于 LLaMA 2-3x\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-type F1 vs BCS scatter (both models) — Qwen3 负斜率可见，LLaMA 平坦\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA 结果是 worst tier 中最关键的 negative result。cross_model_significant = 1\n      （仅 Qwen3），这意味着 confusability 效应可能是 Qwen3 特有的，而非 LLM IE 的\n      普遍现象。论文必须显著降级 Claim 1 的 generalizability：从 \"confusability\n      independently predicts degradation in training-free LLM IE\" 改为\n      \"confusability sensitivity varies substantially across model families, with\n      Qwen3 showing strong effects (r=0.156) and LLaMA showing weak/null effects\n      (r=0.042)\"。在 worst tier 叙事中，这可 reframe 为解释力：\"prior conflicting\n      findings about schema complexity may be partly explained by model-dependent\n      confusability sensitivity\"——将缺陷转为贡献，但 reviewer 是否买账取决于写作。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-008: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-zero：Qwen3 embedding SCS + graph coloring (τ adaptive,\n      k=1.0) 生成 confusability-minimizing batches，与 single-pass 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # Graph coloring stats\n      graph_stats:\n        threshold_tau: 0.847\n        n_edges: 142\n        edge_density: 0.066\n        chromatic_number: 8\n        avg_batch_size: 8.25\n        max_batch_size: 12\n        min_batch_size: 4\n        max_intra_batch_bcs: 0.842\n      # SDGD-zero results\n      sdgd_zero:\n        f1: 0.367\n        precision: 0.318\n        recall: 0.434\n        pred_gold_ratio: 1.36\n      # Single-pass baseline (from exp003a count_64)\n      single_pass:\n        f1: 0.414\n        precision: 0.648\n        recall: 0.304\n      # Comparison\n      delta_f1_vs_single_pass: -4.7\n      delta_precision: -33.0\n      delta_recall: +13.0\n      # Per-batch breakdown\n      per_batch_f1_range: [0.28, 0.42]\n      per_batch_recall_range: [0.35, 0.52]\n      per_batch_precision_range: [0.22, 0.38]\n      # Merge statistics\n      merge_stats:\n        total_predictions: 4850\n        unique_predictions_after_dedup: 4120\n        cross_batch_span_overlap: 0.08\n        predictions_per_sample_avg: 8.2\n        gold_per_sample_avg: 5.9\n      # API cost\n      api_calls: \"8x single-pass (8000 vs 1000 for 1000 samples)\"\n      wall_clock_multiplier: 6.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-zero 失败的核心机制是 \"disambiguation context loss\"。当 confusable types\n      被分到不同 batch 时，每个 batch 中的模型只看到 pair 的一端。例如 person-other\n      在 batch A，person-politician 在 batch B。处理含政治人物的句子时：\n      \n      - Batch A（有 person-other，无 person-politician）：模型将政治人物标为\n        person-other（因为这是最接近的可用 type）→ FP for person-other\n      - Batch B（有 person-politician，无 person-other）：模型将普通人标为\n        person-politician（同理）→ FP for person-politician\n      \n      merge 后，同一实体可能被两个 batch 分别标为不同 type（cross-batch span overlap\n      8%），评估时只有一个是 TP，另一个是 FP。更严重的是，每个 batch 只有 ~8 types，\n      模型倾向过度提取（pred/gold=1.36 vs single-pass 的 0.47），precision 从 0.648\n      暴跌到 0.318。recall 确实从 0.304 提升到 0.434（smaller batch → 更多 attention\n      给每个 type），但 precision 损失远大于 recall 增益。\n      \n      F1 = 0.367 比 single-pass 的 0.414 低 4.7pp。SDGD 的前提假设（separating\n      confusable types reduces confusion）是错误的——对 LLM 来说，看到 confusable types\n      的完整集合反而帮助 disambiguation。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (Few-NERD, 66 types)\n        | Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | Pred/Gold | API Calls |\n        |-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|-----------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 0.47      | 1x        |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 1.36      | 8x        |\n        | Δ           | -4.7pp| -33.0pp   | +13.0pp| +0.89     | +7x       |\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero Per-Batch Breakdown (top 4 batches)\n        | Batch | Types | Avg BCS | F1    | Recall | Precision |\n        |-------|-------|---------|-------|--------|-----------|\n        | 0     | 12    | 0.812   | 0.42  | 0.48   | 0.38      |\n        | 1     | 10    | 0.795   | 0.38  | 0.45   | 0.33      |\n        | 2     | 9     | 0.780   | 0.35  | 0.42   | 0.30      |\n        | 3     | 8     | 0.763   | 0.32  | 0.40   | 0.27      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SDGD-zero vs single-pass P/R/F1 bar chart — precision 暴跌，recall 小幅提升，net F1 下降\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-batch F1 distribution (box plot) — batch 间方差大，最差 batch F1=0.28\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-batch span overlap analysis — 8% 的 span 被多个 batch 提取为不同 type\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-zero 的失败是 worst tier 的核心 negative result。直接否定 Claim 3。\n      failure mode 清晰且可解释：separating confusable types 剥夺了模型的 comparative\n      disambiguation 能力。这是一个 informative negative result——它揭示了 LLM IE 中\n      type co-presence 的 dual role：(1) 增加 confusability（hypothesis 的前提），\n      (2) 提供 disambiguation context（SDGD 未预见的副作用）。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      这个发现可以作为论文的一个 insight：\"confusability is a two-edged sword — the\n      same type co-presence that causes confusion also enables disambiguation\"，\n      解释为什么简单的 separation strategy 不 work。但这最多放在 Discussion section，\n      不能作为 core contribution。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-009: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-zero on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN（168 event types）上的 SDGD-zero。用 adaptive threshold (k=1.0) 生成\n      confusability-minimizing batches。跨任务（NER→ED）验证 SDGD。\n    expected_results:\n      graph_stats:\n        embedding: qwen3\n        scs_mean: 0.216\n        scs_std: 0.103\n        threshold_tau: 0.319\n        n_edges: 1850\n        edge_density: 0.132\n        chromatic_number: 15\n        avg_batch_size: 11.2\n        min_batch_size: 5\n        max_batch_size: 18\n      sdgd_zero:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.168\n        exact_f1: 0.012\n        relaxed_recall: 0.130\n        relaxed_precision: 0.238\n      single_pass:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.241\n        exact_f1: 0.018\n      delta_relaxed_f1: -7.3\n      api_calls: \"15x single-pass\"\n      wall_clock_multiplier: 12.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 失败更严重（Δ=-7.3pp vs Few-NERD 的 -4.7pp），原因：\n      (1) MAVEN count curve 是上升的——更多 types 帮助模型理解 event ontology，\n      decomposition 直接损害这个优势；(2) adaptive τ=0.319（因 MAVEN Qwen3 SCS\n      分布集中在低值区间），graph 中 edge density=13.2%，coloring 产生 15 个 batch，\n      每个约 11 types——这比 single-pass 的 168 types 少了 93%的 type 上下文；\n      (3) 15 个 batch 意味着 15x API 调用，wall-clock 12.8x 但性能反而更差——\n      cost-quality 全面恶化；(4) MAVEN event trigger 是 verb/nominalization，多个\n      event type 共享同一 trigger word（如 \"attack\" 可以是 Attack 也可以是 Conflict），\n      模型需要看到完整 event taxonomy 才能正确 assign type。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass (MAVEN, 168 types)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Exact F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-----------|----------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | 0.018    | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 0.012    | 15x       | 12.8x      |\n        | Δ           | -7.3pp    | -0.6pp   | +14x      | +11.8x     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SDGD-zero vs single-pass on MAVEN — 性能更差且 cost 更高，全面失败\"\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN batch count vs performance — 随着 batch 数量增加性能持续下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN SDGD-zero 是最差的结果之一。15x API cost 换来 -7.3pp 性能下降。\n      与 Few-NERD 的 SDGD 失败共同构成 Claim 3 的致命反证：SDGD 在两个任务上\n      都差于 single-pass，且效果 consistent（方向一致、机制相同）。在 worst tier\n      叙事中，SDGD 相关实验（exp-008, 009, 010, 011, 013, 014）全部降级为 appendix\n      中的 negative result case study，正文仅用 1-2 段文字总结 \"we also explored\n      confusability-minimizing decomposition, which failed because...\"。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-010: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD 上的 SDGD-cal：用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion\n      matrix，替代 embedding SCS。与 SDGD-zero 和 single-pass 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_stats:\n        n_calibration_samples: 8\n        calibration_api_calls: 8\n        empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero: 85\n        spearman_vs_embedding_scs: 0.125\n        p_vs_embedding_scs: 0.031\n      graph_stats:\n        threshold_tau: \"adaptive on empirical confusion\"\n        n_edges: 62\n        chromatic_number: 7\n        avg_batch_size: 9.4\n      sdgd_cal:\n        f1: 0.381\n        precision: 0.342\n        recall: 0.430\n        pred_gold_ratio: 1.26\n      comparison:\n        vs_single_pass_delta: -3.3\n        vs_sdgd_zero_delta: +1.4\n        vs_random_delta: +0.7\n        vs_random_p: 0.58\n      single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      sdgd_zero_f1: 0.367\n      random_f1: 0.374\n    result_rationale: >\n      SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 好（+1.4pp），因为 empirical confusion matrix 比 embedding\n      SCS 更准确地反映实际 model confusion：(1) 非零 confusion pair 只有 85 对（vs\n      embedding SCS 的 142 条 edge），graph 更稀疏 → 7 个 batch（vs 8 个），每个\n      batch 更大 → 更多 type 上下文；(2) calibration 捕捉到一些 embedding SCS 预测不\n      到的 confusion pattern（如语义不近但 surface form 相似的 type pair）。但 SDGD-cal\n      仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp，因为 decomposition 的核心问题（disambiguation context\n      loss）不因 confusion matrix 质量改善而消失。与 random batching 的差异仅 +0.7pp\n      (p=0.58)，不显著——confusability-aware grouping 即使用了 empirical data 也没有\n      显著优势。calibration 的额外 cost（8 次 API 调用）换来的 improvement 微乎其微。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD-cal vs Baselines (Few-NERD)\n        | Method      | F1    | Δ vs SP | Precision | Recall | API Overhead   |\n        |-------------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|----------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | —       | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x             |\n        | Random (k=8)| 0.374 | -4.0    | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x             |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | -4.7    | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x             |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | -3.3    | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x + 8 calib   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Method comparison bar chart (F1) — 所有 decomposition 方法均低于 single-pass\"\n      - \"Fig: Empirical confusion vs embedding SCS scatter — 弱正相关 ρ=0.125\"\n    analysis: >\n      SDGD-cal 是 SDGD 方法线的 \"best effort\"——用 ground truth confusion 替代 proxy。\n      即使如此仍低于 single-pass 3.3pp。这最终否定了 confusability-minimizing\n      decomposition 的整体方法路线：问题不在 confusion matrix 的质量，而在于\n      decomposition 本身损害了 LLM 的 disambiguation context。在 worst tier 叙事中，\n      SDGD-cal 的 marginal improvement over SDGD-zero 可作为 exp-015（SCS validation）\n      的间接证据：embedding proxy 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），但这\n      不是失败的主因——即使 perfect confusion matrix 也不能拯救 decomposition strategy。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-011: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"SDGD-cal on MAVEN\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      MAVEN（168 types）上的 SDGD-cal：empirical confusion matrix + graph coloring。\n      Full comparison table。\n    expected_results:\n      calibration_stats:\n        n_calibration_samples: 10\n        empirical_confusion_pairs_nonzero: 210\n      graph_stats:\n        chromatic_number: 12\n        avg_batch_size: 14.0\n      sdgd_cal:\n        relaxed_f1: 0.188\n        exact_f1: 0.014\n      comparison:\n        vs_single_pass_delta: -5.3\n        vs_sdgd_zero_delta: +2.0\n        vs_random_delta: +0.8\n        vs_random_p: 0.62\n      single_pass_relaxed_f1: 0.241\n      sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.168\n      random_relaxed_f1: 0.180\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Few-NERD 相同模式：SDGD-cal 好于 SDGD-zero（+2.0pp）但仍远差于 single-pass\n      （-5.3pp）。MAVEN 的 empirical confusion matrix 更密（210 nonzero pairs vs\n      Few-NERD 的 85），因为 168 types 中很多 event type 确实会互相 confuse（尤其是\n      同一 FrameNet frame 下的 sibling types）。但 calibration 帮助有限——核心问题\n      仍然是 MAVEN 的性能与 type count 正相关，decomposition 损害性能。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Full Comparison (MAVEN, 168 types, relaxed matching)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | Δ vs SP | API Calls      |\n        |-------------|-----------|---------|----------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | —       | 1x             |\n        | Random (k=12)| 0.180    | -6.1    | 12x            |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | -7.3    | 15x            |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | -5.3    | 12x + 10 calib |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: MAVEN full comparison bar chart — single-pass 远超所有 decomposition 方法\"\n    analysis: >\n      MAVEN SDGD-cal 确认 decomposition 在 event detection 上全面失败。所有方法\n      均差于 single-pass，且 MAVEN 的差距（5-7pp）比 Few-NERD（3-5pp）更大。\n      这强化了 worst tier 的核心结论：decomposition 不是通用 solution，type co-presence\n      在很多场景中是 feature 而非 bug。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-013: Random Batching Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Random Batching Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      与 SDGD-zero 相同 batch 数量 k，随机分组。隔离 confusability-aware grouping\n      的价值（排除 batch count reduction 的贡献）。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd:\n        random_f1: 0.374\n        sdgd_zero_f1: 0.367\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: -0.7\n        paired_t_p: 0.68\n        n_random_seeds: 10\n        random_f1_std: 0.018\n        random_f1_range: [0.348, 0.402]\n        single_pass_f1: 0.414\n      maven:\n        random_relaxed_f1: 0.180\n        sdgd_zero_relaxed_f1: 0.168\n        delta_sdgd_vs_random: -1.2\n        paired_t_p: 0.42\n        n_random_seeds: 5\n      interpretation:\n        sdgd_vs_random_significant: false\n        confusability_aware_grouping_benefit: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Random batching 在 10 个 random seeds 上平均 F1=0.374（std=0.018），而 SDGD-zero\n      F1=0.367。SDGD 比 random 差 0.7pp（p=0.68），差异不显著。实际上 SDGD 可能略\n      差于 random，因为 SDGD 刻意将 confusable types 分开——这意味着每个 batch 内的\n      types 都是 semantically distant 的，模型缺乏同一 semantic cluster 的 types\n      作为 disambiguation anchor。Random batching 偶尔会把 confusable types 放在一起\n      （概率约 1/k），这些 batch 的 disambiguation 更好，平均下来 random 反而略优。\n      \n      在 MAVEN 上同样：random F1=0.180 vs SDGD F1=0.168（Δ=-1.2pp, p=0.42）。\n      SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不仅无益，可能有害。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (Few-NERD, k=8)\n        | Method     | Mean F1 | Std   | Range         | vs Single-Pass |\n        |------------|---------|-------|---------------|----------------|\n        | Random×10  | 0.374   | 0.018 | [0.348,0.402] | -4.0pp         |\n        | SDGD-zero  | 0.367   | —     | —             | -4.7pp         |\n        | Δ (SDGD-Random) | -0.7pp | — | —           | p=0.68 (NS)    |\n      - |\n        Table: Random vs SDGD-zero (MAVEN, k=15/12)\n        | Method     | Relaxed F1 | vs Single-Pass |\n        |------------|-----------|----------------|\n        | Random×5   | 0.180     | -6.1pp         |\n        | SDGD-zero  | 0.168     | -7.3pp         |\n        | Δ          | -1.2pp    | p=0.42 (NS)    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Random batching F1 distribution (violin plot, 10 seeds) with SDGD-zero point overlaid — SDGD 在 random 的分布内\"\n      - \"Fig: Paired comparison scatter (random seed F1 vs SDGD F1) — 大多数 random seed 优于 SDGD\"\n    analysis: >\n      Random batching ablation 是 Claim 3 的 definitive kill shot。SDGD 不显著优于\n      random→confusability-aware grouping 无价值。combined with SDGD < single-pass→\n      decomposition 本身有害。Claim 3 完全不成立。在 worst tier 叙事中，这个实验\n      的 negative result 本身有教育意义：it demonstrates that the intuitive principle\n      \"separate confusable types\" is wrong for LLM IE，因为 LLMs 使用 type co-presence\n      做 comparative reasoning。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-014: Per-Type Splitting Ablation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Per-Type Splitting (UniNER-style) Ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      1 type per batch（k=66/168）。Decomposition 的上界。揭示 latency-quality tradeoff。\n    expected_results:\n      fewnerd:\n        per_type_f1: 0.330\n        per_type_precision: 0.225\n        per_type_recall: 0.620\n        api_calls: \"66x single-pass\"\n        wall_clock_multiplier: 48.0\n      maven:\n        per_type_relaxed_f1: 0.108\n        api_calls: \"168x single-pass\"\n        wall_clock_multiplier: 135.0\n      comparison_fewnerd:\n        single_pass: 0.414\n        sdgd_zero: 0.367\n        random: 0.374\n        per_type: 0.330\n      ordering: \"single-pass > random ≈ SDGD-zero > per-type\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Per-type splitting 是 decomposition 的极端形式：每个 batch 只有 1 个 type。\n      这完全消除 type confusion（BCS=0），但也完全消除 disambiguation context。\n      \n      Few-NERD 结果（F1=0.330）几乎等于 exp003a count_1 的 F1=0.323——符合预期，\n      因为 per-type extraction 本质就是 count=1。precision 极低（0.225）因为模型\n      只知道一个 type，会把任何像样的 span 都标为该 type（massive over-extraction）。\n      recall 最高（0.620）因为模型 aggressively 搜索这个 type 的所有 instance。\n      \n      MAVEN 更惨（relaxed F1=0.108），因为 MAVEN 的 count_1 relaxed_F1 就只有 0.098。\n      168x API 调用使 wall-clock time 完全不可接受。\n      \n      排序 single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 证明：decomposition granularity\n      与性能成反比。batch 越大越好（更多 type context），单pass 最优。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Full Method Comparison (Few-NERD)\n        | Method      | F1    | Precision | Recall | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-------|-----------|--------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.414 | 0.648     | 0.304  | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.381 | 0.342     | 0.430  | 7x        | 5.5x       |\n        | Random (k=8)| 0.374 | 0.335     | 0.425  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.367 | 0.318     | 0.434  | 8x        | 6.5x       |\n        | Per-type    | 0.330 | 0.225     | 0.620  | 66x       | 48x        |\n      - |\n        Table: Full Method Comparison (MAVEN, relaxed)\n        | Method      | Relaxed F1 | API Calls | Wall-Clock |\n        |-------------|-----------|-----------|------------|\n        | Single-pass | 0.241     | 1x        | 1x         |\n        | SDGD-cal    | 0.188     | 12x       | 10x        |\n        | Random      | 0.180     | 12x       | 10x        |\n        | SDGD-zero   | 0.168     | 15x       | 12.8x      |\n        | Per-type    | 0.108     | 168x      | 135x       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: F1 vs API cost Pareto frontier — single-pass 是 Pareto optimal，所有 decomposition 方法 dominated\"\n      - \"Fig: Precision-Recall tradeoff by method — decomposition 方法在 high-recall low-precision 角落\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-type ablation 完成了 decomposition failure 的完整图景。方法排序\n      single-pass > random ≈ SDGD > per-type 说明：(1) decomposition granularity\n      与 F1 反相关；(2) type co-presence 是 net positive（disambiguation > confusion）；\n      (3) SDGD 的 confusability-aware grouping 不提供额外价值（≈ random）。\n      在 worst tier 叙事中，这个结果可 reframe 为 empirical finding：\"LLM IE\n      benefits from full schema visibility; type co-presence enables comparative\n      reasoning that outweighs confusability-induced errors\"——这本身是一个有价值\n      的 insight，但不是 method contribution。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # exp-015: SCS Validation\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Embedding SCS vs Empirical Confusion Validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-015\"\n    description: >\n      计算 embedding SCS（Qwen3 / MiniLM）与 empirical confusion matrix 之间的\n      rank correlation。验证 embedding proxy 对实际 model confusion 的预测力。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.125\n        p: 0.031\n        kendall_tau: 0.092\n        p_kendall: 0.044\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 85\n      minilm_scs_vs_empirical:\n        spearman_rho: 0.098\n        p: 0.082\n        kendall_tau: 0.071\n        p_kendall: 0.115\n        n_pairs_with_confusion: 85\n      top_confused_pair_scs_rank:\n        person_other_politician:\n          scs_rank: 3\n          confusion_rank: 1\n        building_other_library:\n          scs_rank: 45\n          confusion_rank: 8\n          comment: \"high confusion, low SCS — embedding 未捕捉的 confusion pattern\"\n      scs_false_positive_rate: 0.42\n      scs_false_negative_rate: 0.35\n    result_rationale: >\n      Embedding SCS 与 empirical confusion 仅弱相关（ρ=0.125），原因：(1) embedding\n      similarity 反映 semantic proximity，但 model confusion 还受 surface form\n      similarity、type definition wording、in-context position 等因素影响——这些因素\n      与 embedding space 正交；(2) SCS 是对称的（sim(A,B)=sim(B,A)），但实际 confusion\n      是非对称的（person-other → person-politician 的概率可能远高于反向）；(3) 42%\n      的 false positive rate 意味着 SCS 预测为 confusable 的 type pair 中近一半实际\n      不被 confuse——这些 false alarm 导致 SDGD-zero 过度分离 types，graph 变密，\n      batch 数量过多。\n      \n      MiniLM SCS 更差（ρ=0.098, p=0.082），因为 MiniLM 是 general-purpose sentence\n      embedding，不 align 到 Qwen3 的 internal representation。这解释了为什么\n      extraction model alignment 对 per-type signal 很重要（exp-002 中 Qwen3 per-type\n      ρ=-0.293 vs MiniLM ρ≈0）。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Correlation\n        | Embedding | Spearman ρ | p     | Kendall τ | p     |\n        |-----------|-----------|-------|-----------|-------|\n        | Qwen3     | 0.125     | 0.031 | 0.092     | 0.044 |\n        | MiniLM    | 0.098     | 0.082 | 0.071     | 0.115 |\n      - |\n        Table: SCS Proxy Error Analysis\n        | Metric              | Qwen3 | MiniLM |\n        |---------------------|-------|--------|\n        | False Positive Rate | 0.42  | 0.48   |\n        | False Negative Rate | 0.35  | 0.40   |\n        | Top-1 Match         | Yes   | No     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (Qwen3) — 弱正相关，大量 off-diagonal noise\"\n      - \"Fig: Confusion asymmetry heatmap — 展示 confusion matrix 的非对称性，SCS 无法捕捉\"\n    analysis: >\n      SCS validation 结果解释了 SDGD 失败的一个次要原因（proxy 质量差），但不是主因\n      （主因是 decomposition 本身有害）。ρ=0.125 说明 embedding SCS 只能解释 ~1.6%\n      的 confusion variance——作为 graph 构建的基础远远不够。即使用 empirical confusion\n      (exp-010 SDGD-cal) 也只比 random 好 0.7pp（不显著），所以 proxy 质量不是瓶颈。\n      在 worst tier 叙事中，SCS validation 作为 methodological finding 报告：\n      \"embedding-based confusability proxies have limited predictive power for actual\n      model confusion patterns, suggesting that confusability is mediated by factors\n      beyond semantic similarity\"——这对未来工作有指导价值。\n\n  ##############################################################################\n  # Summary tables for paper\n  ##############################################################################\n  - name: \"Cross-Experiment Summary (for paper narrative)\"\n    plan_id: \"summary\"\n    description: >\n      综合所有实验的 worst tier 结果，构建论文核心 tables 和 narrative。\n    expected_results:\n      # Claim 1 summary\n      claim1_pairwise_matrix:\n        qwen3_fewnerd: \"r=0.156*** ✓\"\n        qwen3_maven: \"r=-0.009 (ns) ✗\"\n        qwen3_fewrel: \"pending\"\n        minilm_fewnerd: \"not tested\"\n        minilm_maven: \"r=0.115*** ✓\"\n        minilm_fewrel: \"Δ=21-50pp ✓ (pilot)\"\n        llama_fewnerd: \"r=0.042 (ns) ✗\"\n        significant_cells: 3\n        total_cells: 7\n        verdict: \"partial — 3/7 significant, no single embedding/model universally works\"\n      # Claim 2 summary\n      claim2_evidence:\n        count_recall_monotonic: true\n        bcs_type_substitution_ratio_extreme: \"4.8x\"\n        bcs_type_substitution_ratio_random: \"1.5x\"\n        interaction_significant: false\n        error_taxonomy_dominant_mode: \"spurious extraction (45%), not type confusion (18%)\"\n        verdict: \"directional — channels exist but confusability channel is weak relative to other error sources\"\n      # Claim 3 summary\n      claim3_evidence:\n        sdgd_zero_fewnerd: \"F1=0.367, Δ=-4.7pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_zero_maven: \"relF1=0.168, Δ=-7.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_cal_fewnerd: \"F1=0.381, Δ=-3.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_cal_maven: \"relF1=0.188, Δ=-5.3pp vs SP\"\n        sdgd_vs_random_significant: false\n        per_type_worst: true\n        verdict: \"FAILED — all decomposition methods inferior to single-pass\"\n      # Paper structure\n      recommended_paper_structure:\n        - \"1. Introduction: 'What makes schemas complex for LLMs?'\"\n        - \"2. Related Work: decomposition approaches + empirical studies\"\n        - \"3. Experimental Setup: 3 tasks, 2 models, 2 embeddings\"\n        - \"4. Finding 1: Pairwise confusability predicts type confusion (model-dependent)\"\n        - \"5. Finding 2: Count and confusability act through distinguishable channels\"\n        - \"6. Finding 3: Per-type aggregation introduces centrality confound\"\n        - \"7. Finding 4: Confusability-minimizing decomposition fails (negative result)\"\n        - \"8. Discussion: implications for future work\"\n        - \"9. Conclusion\"\n      recommended_venue: \"EMNLP 2026 Findings (realistic), Main (stretch)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst tier 总体图景：论文有两个可靠发现（pairwise confusability signal on\n      Qwen3×FewNERD + MiniLM×MAVEN；centrality confound on MAVEN）和一系列 informative\n      negative results（LLaMA 无信号、SDGD 全面失败、interaction 不显著）。叙事必须\n      从 \"we discover and exploit confusability\" 彻底转为 \"we systematically investigate\n      schema complexity, finding that confusability effects are real but model-dependent,\n      and that the intuitive decomposition strategy fails because LLMs need type\n      co-presence for disambiguation\"。这种 \"honest empirical study with negative\n      results\" 的论文在 EMNLP Findings 有先例（如 \"Do Prompt-Based Models Really\n      Understand the Meaning of Their Prompts?\" ACL 2022），但需要极强的写作功力\n      和清晰的 takeaway。\n    tables:\n      - |\n        Table: Pairwise SCS-Confusion Signal (Cross-Task × Cross-Model × Cross-Embedding)\n        | Model  | Embedding | Few-NERD (NER) | MAVEN (ED) | FewRel (RE) |\n        |--------|-----------|----------------|------------|-------------|\n        | Qwen3  | Qwen3     | r=0.156***     | r=-0.009   | —           |\n        | Qwen3  | MiniLM    | —              | r=0.115*** | Δ=21-50pp*  |\n        | LLaMA  | Qwen3     | r=0.042        | —          | —           |\n        *** p<0.001, * pilot only\n      - |\n        Table: SDGD Full Comparison (worst tier)\n        | Method       | Few-NERD F1 | Δ vs SP | MAVEN relF1 | Δ vs SP |\n        |-------------|-------------|---------|-------------|---------|\n        | Single-pass  | 0.414       | —       | 0.241       | —       |\n        | SDGD-cal     | 0.381       | -3.3    | 0.188       | -5.3    |\n        | Random (=k)  | 0.374       | -4.0    | 0.180       | -6.1    |\n        | SDGD-zero    | 0.367       | -4.7    | 0.168       | -7.3    |\n        | Per-type     | 0.330       | -8.4    | 0.108       | -13.3   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 论文 hero figure — schema complexity 的 multi-dimensional decomposition (count × confusability × model)，展示不同维度的 effect 和 interaction\"\n      - \"Fig: Cross-experiment evidence summary — 3×3 grid 展示 task × model × embedding 的 signal 有无\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst tier 论文的核心卖点不是 positive findings 而是 systematic methodology\n      和 honest reporting。三个 takeaway：(1) confusability 信号存在但\n      model/embedding-dependent——未来工作不能假设 universal confusability measure；\n      (2) per-type 聚合有 centrality confound——未来工作应使用 pairwise 分析；\n      (3) confusability-minimizing decomposition 失败——LLM 需要 type co-presence\n      做 comparative reasoning，简单分离策略适得其反。这些 negative-but-informative\n      results 加上 controlled experimental design 可以支撑一篇 Findings paper。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d6066cd7-3b7c-4597-bdab-f4c39ace5902","total_cost_usd":1.30677925,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46307,"cache_read_input_tokens":85395,"output_tokens":38466,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":26426,"cache_read_input_tokens":43817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":12853,"outputTokens":28,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.01299